3 Kings	3Ki	11	16	34	In his days Hiel of Bethel built Jericho: in Abiram his firstborn he laid its foundations: and in his youngest son Segub he set up the gates thereof: according to the word of the Lord, which he spoke in the hand of Josue the son of Nun.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	1	And Elias the Thesbite of the inhabitants of Galaad said to Achab: As the Lord liveth the God of Israel, in whose sight I stand, there shall not be dew nor rain these years, but according to the words of my mouth.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	2	And the word of the Lord came to him, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	3	Get thee hence, and go towards the east and hide thyself by the torrent of Carith, which is over against the Jordan,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	4	And there thou shalt drink of the torrent: and I have commanded the ravens to feed thee there.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	5	So he went, and did according to the word of the Lord: and going, he dwelt by the torrent Carith, which is over against the Jordan.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	6	And the ravens brought him bread and flesh in the morning, and bread and flesh in the evening, and he drank of the torrent.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	7	But after some time the torrent was dried up, for it had not rained upon the earth.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	8	Then the word of the Lord came to him, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	9	Arise, and go to Sarephta of the Sidonians, and dwell there: for I have commanded a widow woman there to feed thee.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	17	10	He arose, and went to Sarephta. And when he was come to the gate of the city, he saw the widow woman gathering sticks, and he called her, and said to her: Give me a little water in a vessel, that I may drink.
