3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	8	So she wrote letter's in Achab's name, and sealed them with his ring, and sent them to the ancients, and the chief men that were in his city, and that dwelt with Naboth.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	9	And this was the tenor of the letters: Proclaim a fast, and make Naboth sit among the chief of the people,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	10	And suborn two men, sons of Belial against him, and let them bear false witness: that he hath blasphemed God and the king: and then carry him out, and stone him, and so let him die.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	11	And the men of his city, the ancients and nobles, that dwelt with him in the city, did as Jezabel had commanded them, and as it was written in the letters which she had sent to them:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	12	They proclaimed a fast, and made Naboth sit among the chief of the people.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	13	And bringing two men, sons of the devil, they made them sit against him: and they, like men of the devil, bore witness against him before the people, saying: Naboth hath blasphemed God and the king: wherefore they brought him forth without the city, and stoned him to death.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	14	And they sent to Jezabel, saying: Naboth is stoned, and is dead.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	15	And it came to pass when Jezabel heard that Naboth was stoned, and dead, that she said to Achab: Arise and take possession of the vineyard of Naboth the Jezrahelite, who would not agree with thee, and give it thee for money: for Naboth is not alive, but dead.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	16	And when Achab heard this, to wit, that Naboth was dead, he arose, and went down to the vineyard of Naboth the Jezrahelite, to take possession of it.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	17	And the word of the Lord came to Elias the Thesbite, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	18	Arise, and go down to meet Achab king of Israel, who is in Samaria: behold he is going down to the vineyard of Naboth, to take possession of it:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	19	And thou shalt speak to him, saying: Thus saith the Lord: Thou hast slain, moreover also thou hast taken possession. And after these words thou shalt add: Thus saith the Lord: In this place, wherein the dogs have licked the blood of Naboth, they shall lick thy blood also.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	20	And Achab said to Elias: Hast thou found me thy enemy? He said: I have found thee, because thou art sold, to do evil in the sight of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	21	Behold I will bring evil upon thee, and I will cut down thy posterity, and I will kill of Achab him that pisseth against the wall, and him that is shut up, and the last in Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	22	And I will make thy house like the house of Jeroboam the son of Nabat, and like the house of Baasa the son of Ahias: for what thou hast done, to provoke me to anger, and for making Israel to sin.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	23	And of Jezabel also the Lord spoke, saying: The dogs shall eat Jezabel in the field of Jezrahel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	24	If Achab die in the city, the dogs shall eat him: but if he die in the field, the birds of the air shall eat him.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	25	Now there was not such another as Achab, who was sold to do evil in the sight of the Lord: for his wife Jezabel set him on,
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	26	And he became abominable, insomuch that he followed the idols which the Amorrhites had made, whom the Lord destroyed before the face of the children of Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	27	And when Achab had heard these words, he rent his garments, and put haircloth upon his flesh, and fasted and slept in sackcloth, and walked with his head cast down.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	28	And the word of the Lord came to Elias the Thesbite, saying:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	21	29	Hast thou not seen Achab humbled before me? therefore, because he hath humbled himself for my sake, I will not bring the evil in his days, but in his son's days will I bring the evil upon his house.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	1	And there passed three years without war between Syria and Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	2	And in the third year, Josaphat king of Juda came down to the king of Israel.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	3	(And the king of Israel said to his servants: Know ye not-that Ramoth Galaad is ours, and we neglect to take it out of the hand of the king of Syria?)
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	4	And he said to Josaphat: Wilt thou come with me to battle to Ramoth Galaad?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	5	And Josaphat said to the king of Israel: As I am, so art thou: my people and thy people are one: and my horsemen, thy horsemen. And Josaphat said to the king of Israel: Inquire, I beseech thee, this day, the word of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	6	Then the king of Israel assembled the prophets, about four hundred men, and he said to them: Shall I go to Ramoth Galaad to fight, or shall I forbear? They answered: Go up, and the Lord will deliver it into the hand of the king.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	7	And Josaphat said: Is there not here some prophet of the Lord, that we may inquire by him?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	8	And the king of Israel said to Josaphat: There is one man left, by whom we may inquire of the Lord: Micheas the son of Jemla; but I hate him, for he doth not prophesy good to me, but evil. And Josaphat said: Speak not so, O king.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	9	Then the king of Israel called an eunuch, and said to him: Make haste, and bring hither Micheas the son of Jemla.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	10	Then the king of Israel, and Josaphat king of Juda, sat each on his throne clothed with royal robes, in a court by the entrance of the gate of Samaria, and all the prophets prophesied before them.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	11	And Sedecias the son of Chanaana made himself horns of iron, and said: Thus saith the Lord: With these shalt thou push Syria, till thou destroy it.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	12	And all the prophets prophesied in like manner, saying: Go up to Ramoth Galaad, and prosper, for the Lord will deliver it into the king's hands.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	13	And the messenger, that went to call Micheas, spoke to him, saying: Behold the words of the prophets with one mouth declare good things to the king: let thy word therefore be like to theirs, and speak that which is good.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	14	But Micheas said to him: As the Lord liveth, whatsoever the Lord shall say to me, that will I speak.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	15	So he came to the king, and the king said to him: Micheas, shall we go to Ramoth Galaad to battle, or shall we forbear? He answered him: Go up, and prosper, and the Lord shall deliver it into the king's hands.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	16	But the king said to him: I adjure thee again and again, that thou tell me nothing but that which is true in the name of the Lord.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	17	And he said: I saw all Israel scattered upon the hills, like sheep that have no shepherd: and the Lord said: These have no master: let every man of them return to his house in peace.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	18	(Then the king of Israel said to Josaphat: Did I not tell thee, that he prophesieth no good to me, but always evil?)
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	19	And he added and said: Hear thou therefore the word of the Lord: I saw the Lord sitting on his throne, and all the army of heaven standing by him on the right hand and on the left:
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	20	And the Lord said: Who shall deceive Achab king of Israel, that he may go up, and fall at Ramoth Galaad? And one spoke words of this manner, and another otherwise.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	21	And there came forth a spirit, and stood before the Lord, and said: I will deceive him. And the Lord said to him: By what means?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	22	And he said: I will go forth, and be a lying spirit in the mouth of all his prophets. And the Lord said: Thou shalt deceive him, and shalt prevail: a go forth, and do so.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	23	Now therefore behold the Lord hath given a lying spirit in the mouth of all thy prophets that are here, and the Lord hath spoken evil against thee.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	24	And Sedecias the son of Chanaana came, and struck Micheas on the cheek, and said: Hath then the spirit of the Lord left me, and spoken to thee?
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	25	And Micheas said: Thou shalt see in the day when thou shalt go into a chamber within a chamber to hide thyself.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	26	And the king of Israel said: Take Micheas, and let him abide with Ammon the governor of the city, and with Joas the son of Amalech.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	27	And tell them: Thus saith the king: Put this man in prison, and feed him with bread of affliction, and water of distress, till I return in peace.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	28	And Micheas said: If thou return in peace, the Lord hath not spoken by me. And he said: Hear, all ye people.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	29	So the king of Israel, and Josaphat king of Juda went up to Ramoth Galaad.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	30	And the king of Israel said to Josaphat: Take armour, and go into the battle, and put on thy own garments. But the king of Israel changed his dress, and went into the battle.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	31	And the king of Syria had commanded the two and thirty captains of the chariots, saying: You shall not fight against any, small or great, but against the king of Israel only.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	32	So when the captains of the chariots saw Josaphat, they suspected that he was the king of Israel, and making a violent assault they fought against him: and Josaphat cried out.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	33	And the captains of the chariots perceived that he was not the king of Israel, and they turned away from him.
3 Kings	3Ki	11	22	34	And a certain man bent his bow, shooting at a venture, and chanced to strike the king of Israel between the lungs and the stomach. But he said to the driver of his chariot: Turn thy hand, and carry me out of the army, for I am grievously wounded.
