4 Kings	4Ki	12	13	25	Now Joas the son of Joachaz, took the cities out of the hand of Benadad, the son of Hazael, which he had taken out of the hand of Joachaz his father by war, three times did Joas beat him, and he restored the cities to Israel.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	1	In the second year of Joas son of Joachaz, king of Israel, reigned Amasias son of Joas king of Juda.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	2	He was five and twenty years old when he began to reign: and nine and twenty years he reigned in Jerusalem: the name of his mother was Joadan of Jerusalem.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	3	And he did that which was right before the Lord, but yet not like David his father. He did according to all things that Joas his father did:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	4	But this only, that he took not away the high places: for yet the people sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	5	And when he had possession of the kingdom, he put his servants to death that had slain the king his father:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	6	But the children of the murderers he did not put to death, according to that which is written in the book of the law of Moses, wherein the Lord commanded, saying: The fathers shall not be put to death for the children, neither shall the children be put to death for the fathers: but every man shall die for his own sins.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	7	He slew of Edom in the valley of the Saltpits ten thousand men, and took the rock by war, and called the name thereof Jectehel, unto this day.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	8	Then Amasias sent messengers to Joas son of Joachaz, son of Jehu king of Israel, saying: Come let us see one another.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	9	And Joas king of Israel sent again to Amasias king of Juda, saying: A thistle of Libanus sent to a cedar tree, which is in Libanus, saying: Give thy daughter to my son to wife. And the beasts of the forest, that are in Libanus, passed and trod down the thistle.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	10	Thou hast beaten and prevailed over Edom, and thy heart hath lifted thee up: be content with the glory, and sit at home: why provokest thou evil, that thou shouldst fall, and Juda with thee?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	11	But Amasias did not rest satisfied. So Joas king of Israel went up, and he and Amasias king of Juda saw one another in Bethsames a town in Juda.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	12	And Juda was put to the worst before Israel, and they fled every man to their dwellings.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	13	But Joas king of Israel took Amasias, king of Juda the son of Joas, the son of Ochozias, in Bethsames, and brought him into Jerusalem: and he broke down the wall of Jerusalem, from the gate of Ephraim to the gate of the corner, four hundred cubits.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	14	And he took all the gold, and silver, and all the vessels, that were found in the house of the Lord, and in the king's treasures, and hostages, and returned to Samaria.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	15	But the rest of the acts of Joas, which he did, and his valour, wherewith he fought against Amasias king of Juda, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Israel?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	16	And Joas slept with his fathers, and was buried in Samaria, with the kings of Israel: and Jeroboam his son reigned in his stead.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	17	And Amasias the son of Joas king of Juda lived, after the death of Joas son of Joachaz king of Israel fifteen years.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	18	And the rest of the acts of Amasias, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Juda?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	19	Now they made a conspiracy against him in Jerusalem: and he fled to Lachis. And they sent after him to Lachis, and killed him there.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	20	And they brought him away upon horses, and he was buried in Jerusalem with his fathers in the city of David.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	21	And all the people of Juda took Azarias, who was sixteen years old, and made him king instead of his father Amasias.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	22	He built Elath, and restored it to Juda, after that the king slept with his fathers.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	23	In the fifteenth year of Amasias son of Joas king of Juda, reigned Jeroboam the son of Joas king of Israel in Samaria, one and forty years:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	24	And he did that which was evil before the Lord. He departed not from all the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nabat, who made Israel to sin.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	25	He restored the borders of Israel from the entrance of Emath, unto the sea of the wilderness, according to the word of the Lord the God of Israel, which he spoke by his servant Jonas the son of Amathi, the prophet, who was of Geth, which is in Opher.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	26	For the Lord saw the affliction of Israel that it was exceeding bitter, and that they were consumed even to them that were shut up in prison, and the lowest persons, and that there was no one to help Israel.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	27	And the Lord did not say that he would blot out the name of Israel from under heaven, but he saved them by the hand of Jeroboam the son of Joas.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	28	But the rest of the acts of Jeroboam, and all that he did, and his valour, wherewith he fought, and how he restored Damascus, and Emath to Juda in Israel, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Israel?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	14	29	And Jeroboam slept with his fathers the kings of Israel, and Zacharias his son reigned in his stead.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	1	In the seven and twentieth year of Jeroboam king of Israel reigned Azarias son of Amasias, king of Juda.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	2	He was sixteen years old, when he began to reign, and he reigned two and fifty years in Jerusalem: the name of his mother was Jechelia of Jerusalem.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	3	And he did that which was pleasing before the Lord, according to all that his father Amasias had done.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	4	But the high places he did not destroy: for the people sacrificed and burnt incense in the high places.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	5	And the Lord struck the king, so that he was a leper unto the day of his death, and he dwelt in a free house apart: but Joatham the king's soil governed the palace, and judged the people of the land.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	6	And the rest of the acts of Azarias, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Juda?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	7	And Azarias slept with his fathers: and they buried him with his ancestors in the city of David, and Joatham his son reigned in his stead.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	8	In the eight and thirtieth year of Azarias king of Juda, reigned Zacharias son of Jeroboam over Israel in Samaria six months:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	9	And he did that which is evil before the Lord, as his fathers had done: he departed not from the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nabat who made Israel to sin.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	10	And Sellum the son of Jabes conspired against him: and struck him publicly and killed him, and reigned in his place.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	11	Now the rest of the acts of Zacharias, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Israel?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	12	This was the word of the Lord, which he spoke to Jehu, saying: Thy children to the fourth generation shall sit upon the throne of Israel. And so it came to pass.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	13	Sellum the son of Jabes began to reign in the nine and thirtieth year of Azarias king of Juda: and reigned one month in Samaria.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	15	14	And Manahem the son of Gadi went up from Thersa: and he came into Samaria, and struck Sellum the son of Jabes in Samaria, and slew him, and reigned in his stead.
