4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	1	In those days Ezechias was sick unto death: and Isaias the son of Amos the prophet came and said to him: Thus saith the Lord God: Give charge concerning thy house, for thou shalt die, and not live.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	2	And he turned his face to the wall, and prayed to the Lord, saying:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	3	I beseech thee, O Lord, remember how I have walked before thee in truth, and with a perfect heart, and have done that which is pleasing before thee. And Ezechias wept with much weeping.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	4	And before Isaias was gone out of the middle of the court, the word of the Lord came to him, saying:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	5	Go back, and tell Ezechias the captain of my people: Thus saith the Lord the God of David thy father: I have heard thy prayer, and I have seen thy tears: and behold I have healed thee; on the third day thou shalt go up to the temple of the Lord.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	6	And I will add to thy days fifteen years: and I will deliver thee and this city out of the hand of the king of the Assyrians, and I will protect this city for my own sake, and for David my servant's sake.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	7	And Isaias said: Bring me a lump of figs. And when they had brought it, and laid it upon his boil. he was healed.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	8	And Ezechias had said to Isaias: What shall be the sign that the Lord will heal me, and that I shall go up to the temple of the Lord the third day?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	9	And Isaias said to him: This shall be the sign from the Lord, that the Lord will do the word which he hath spoken: Wilt thou that the shadow go forward ten lines, or that it go back so many degrees?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	10	And Ezechias said: It is an easy matter for the shadow to go forward ten lines: and I do not desire that this be done, but let it return back ten degrees.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	11	And Isaias the prophet called upon the Lord, and he brought the shadow ten degrees backwards by the lines, by which it had already gone down in the dial of Achaz.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	12	At that time Berodach Baladan, the son of Baladan, king of the Babylonians, sent letters and presents to Ezechias: for he had heard that Ezechias had been sick.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	13	And Ezechias rejoiced at their coming, and he shewed them the house of his aromatical spices, and the gold and the silver, and divers precious odours, and ointments, and the house of his vessels, and all that he had in his treasures. There was nothing in his house, nor in all his dominions that Ezechias shewed them not.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	14	And Isaias the prophet came to king Ezechias, and said to him: What said these men? or from whence came they to thee? And Ezechias said to him: From a far country they came to me out of Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	20	15	And he said: What did they see in thy house? Ezechias said: They saw all the things that are in my house: there is nothing among my treasures that I have not shewn them.
