4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	23	As was this phase that was kept to the Lord in Jerusalem, in the eighteenth year of king Josias.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	24	Moreover the diviners by spirits, and soothsayers, and the figures of idols, and the uncleannesses, and the abominations, that had been in the land of Juda, and Jerusalem, Josias took away: that he might perform the words of the law, that were written in the book which Helcias the priest had found in the temple of the Lord.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	25	There was no king before him like unto him, that returned to the Lord with all his heart, and with all his soul, and with ail his strength, according to all the law of Moses: neither after him did there arise any like him.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	26	But yet the Lord turned not away from the wrath of his great indignation, wherewith his anger was kindled against Juda: because of the provocations, wherewith Manasses had provoked him.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	27	And the Lord said: I will remove Juda also from before my face, as I have removed Israel: and I will cast off this city Jerusalem, which I chose, and the house, of which I said: My name shall be there.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	28	Now the rest of the acts of Josias, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Juda?
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	29	In his days Pharao Nechao king of Egypt went up against the king of Assyria to the river Euphrates: and king Josias went to meet him: and was slain at Mageddo, when he had seen him.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	30	And his servants carried him dead from Mageddo: and they brought him to Jerusalem, and buried him in Iris own sepulchre. And the people of the land took Joachaz the son of Josias: and they anointed him, and made him king in his father's stead.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	31	Joachaz was three and twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned three months in Jerusalem: the name of his mother was Amital, the daughter of Jeremias of Lobna.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	32	And he did evil before the Lord, according to all that his fathers had done.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	33	And Pharao Nechao bound him at Rebla, which is in the land of Emath, that he should not reign in Jerusalem: and he set a fine upon the land, of a hundred talents of silver, and a talent of gold.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	34	And Pharao Nechao made Eliacim the son of Josias king in the room of Josias his father: and turned his name to Joakim. And he took Joachaz away and carried him into Egypt, and he died there.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	35	And Joakim gave the silver and the gold to Pharao, after he had taxed the land for every man, to contribute according to the commandment of Pharao: and he exacted both the silver and the gold of the people of the land, of every man according to his ability: to give to Pharao Nechao.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	36	Joakim was five and twenty years old when he began to reign: and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem: the name of his mother was Zebida the daughter of Phadaia of Ruma.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	23	37	And he did evil before the Lord according to all that his fathers had done.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	1	In his days Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon came up, and Joakim became his servant three years: then again he rebelled against him.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	2	And the Lord sent against him the rovers of the Chaldees, and the rovers of Syria, and the rovers of Moab, and the rovers of the children of Ammon: and he sent them against Juda, to destroy it, according to the word of the Lord, which he had spoken by his servants the prophets.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	3	And this came by the word of the Lord against Juda, to remove them from before him for all the sins of Manasses which he did.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	4	And for the innocent blood that he shed, filling Jerusalem with innocent blood: and therefore the Lord would not be appeased.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	5	But the rest of the acts of Joakim, and all that he did, are they not written in the book of the words of the days of the kings of Juda? And Joakim slept with his fathers:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	6	And Joachin his son reigned in his stead.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	7	And the king of Egypt came not again any more out of his own country: for the king of Babylon had taken all that had belonged to the king of Egypt, from the river of Egypt, unto the river Euphrates.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	8	Joachin was eighteen years old when he began to reign, a and he reigned three months in Jerusalem: the name of his mother was Nohesta the daughter of Elnathan of Jerusalem.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	9	And he did evil before the Lord, according to all that his father had done.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	10	At that time the servants of Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon came up against Jerusalem, and the city was surrounded with their forts.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	11	And Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon came to the city with his servants to assault it.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	12	And Joachin king of Juda went out to the king of Babylon, he and his mother, and his servants, and his nobles, and his eunuchs: and the king of Babylon received him in the eighth year of his reign.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	13	And he brought out from thence all the treasures of the house of the Lord, and the treasures of the king's house: and he cut in pieces all the vessels of gold which Solomon king of Israel had made in the temple of the Lord, according to the word of the Lord.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	14	And he carried away all Jerusalem, and all the princes, and all the valiant men of the army, to the number of ten thousand into captivity: and every artificer and smith: and none were left, but the poor sort of the people of the land.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	15	And he carried away Joachin into Babylon, and the king's mother, and the king's wives, and his eunuchs: and the judges of the land he carried into captivity from Jerusalem into Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	16	And all the strong men, seven thousand, and the artificers, and the smiths a thousand, all that were valiant men and fit for war: and the king of Babylon led them captives into Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	17	And he appointed Matthanias his uncle in his stead: and called his name Sedecias.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	18	Sedecias was one and twenty years old when he began to reign, and he reigned eleven years in Jerusalem: the name of his mother was Amital, the daughter of Jeremias of Lobna.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	19	And he did evil before the Lord, according to all that Joakim had done.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	24	20	For the Lord was angry against Jerusalem and against Juda, till he cast them out from his face: and Sedecias revolted from the king of Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	1	And it came to pass in the ninth year of his reign, in the tenth month, the tenth day of the month, that Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon came, he and all his army against Jerusalem: and they surrounded it: and raised works round about it.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	2	And the city was shut up and besieged till the eleventh year of king Sedecias,
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	3	The ninth day of the month: and a famine prevailed in the city, and there was no bread for the people of the land.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	4	And a breach was made into the city: and all the men of war fled in the night between the two walls by the king's garden, (now the Chaldees besieged the city round about,) and Sedecias fled by the way that leadeth to the plains of the wilderness.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	5	And the army of the Chaldees pursued after the king, and overtook him in the plains of Jericho: and all the warriors that were with him were scattered, and left him:
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	6	So they took the king, and brought him to the king of Babylon to Reblatha, and he gave judgment upon him.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	7	And he slew the sons of Sedecias before his face, and he put out his eyes, and bound him with chains, and brought him to Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	8	In the fifth month, the seventh day of the month, that is, the nineteenth year of the king of Babylon, came Nabuzardan commander of the army, a servant of the king of Babylon, into Jerusalem.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	9	And he burnt the house of the Lord, and the king's house, and the houses of Jerusalem, and every house he burnt with fire.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	10	And all the army of the Chaldees, which was with the commander of the troops, broke down the walls of Jerusalem round about.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	11	And Nabuzardan the commander of the army, carried away the rest of the people that remained in the city, and the fugitives that had gone over to the king of Babylon, and the remnant of the common people.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	12	But of the poor of the land he left some dressers of vines and husbandmen.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	13	And the pillars of brass that were in the temple of the Lord, and the bases, and the sea of brass which was in the house of the Lord, the Chaldees broke in pieces, and carried all the brass of them to Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	14	They took away also the pots of brass, and the mazers, and the forks, and the cups, and the mortars, and all the vessels of brass with which they ministered.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	15	Moreover also the censers, and the bowls, such as were of gold in gold, and such as were of silver in silver, the general of the army took away.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	16	That is, two pillars, one sea, and the bases which Solomon had made in the temple of the Lord: the brass of all these vessels was without weight.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	17	One pillar was eighteen cubits high, and the chapiter of brass which was upon it was three cubits high: and the network, and the pomegranates that were upon the chapiter of the pillar, were all of brass: and the second pillar had the like adorning.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	18	And the general of the army took Seraias the chief priest, and Sophonias the second priest, and three doorkeepers.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	19	And out of the city one eunuch, who was captain over the men of war: and five men of them that had stood before the king, whom he found in the city, and Sopher the captain of the army who exercised the young soldiers of the people of the land: and threescore men of the common people, who were found in the city.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	20	These Nabuzardan the general of the army took away, and carried them to the king of Babylon to Reblatha.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	21	And the king of Babylon smote them, and slew them at Reblatha in the land of Emath: so Juda was carried away out of their land.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	22	But over the people that remained in the land of Juda, which Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon had left, he gave the government to Godolias the son of Ahicam the son of Saphan.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	23	And when all the captains of the soldiers had heard this, they and the men that were with them, to wit, that the king of Babylon had made Godolias governor, they came to Godolias to Maspha, Ismael the son of Nathanias, and Johanan the son of Caree, and Saraia the son of Thanehumeth the Netophathite, and Jezonias the son of Maachathi, they and their men.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	24	And Godolias swore to them and to their men, saying: Be not afraid to serve the Chaldees: stay in the land, and serve the king of Babylon, and it shall be well with you.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	25	But it came to pass in the seventh month, that Ismael the son of Nathanias, the son of Elisama of the seed royal came, and ten men with him: and smote Godolias so that he died: and also the Jews and the Chaldees that were with him in Maspha.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	26	And all the people both little and great, and the captains of the soldiers, rising up went to Egypt, fearing the Chaldees.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	27	And it came to pass in the seven and thirtieth year of the captivity of Joachin king of Juda, in the twelfth month the seven and twentieth day of the month: Evilmerodach king of Babylon, in the year that he began to reign, lifted up the head of Joachin king of Juda out of prison.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	28	And he spoke kindly to him: and he set his throne above the throne of the kings that were with him in Babylon.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	29	And he changed his garments which he had in prison, and he ate bread always before him, all the days of his life.
4 Kings	4Ki	12	25	30	And he appointed him a continual allowance, which was also given him by the king day by day, all the days of his life.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	1	Adam, Seth, Enos,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	2	Cainan, Malaleel, Jared,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	3	Henoc, Mathusale, Lamech,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	4	Noe, Sem, Cham, and Japheth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	5	The sons of Japheth: Gomer, and Magog, and Madai, and Javan, Thubal, Mosoch, Thiras.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	6	And the sons of Gomer: Ascenez, and Riphath, and Thogorma.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	7	And the sons of Javan: Elisa and Tharsis, Cethim and Dodanim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	8	The sons of Cham: Chus, and Mesrai, and Phut, and Chaanan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	9	And the sons of Chus: Saba, and Hevila, Sabatha, and Regma, and Sabathaca. And the sons of Regma: Saba, and Dadan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	10	Now Chus begot Nemrod: he began to be mighty upon earth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	11	But Mesraim begot Ludim, and Anamim, and Laabim, and Nephtuim,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	12	Phetrusim also, and Casluim: from whom came the Philistines, and Caphtorim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	13	And Chanaan beget Sidon his firstborn, and the Hethite,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	14	And the Jebusite, and the Amorrhite, and the Gergesite,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	15	And the Hevite, and the Aracite, and the Sinite,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	16	And the Aradian, and the Samarite, and the Hamathite.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	17	The sons of Sem: Elam and Asur, and Arphaxad, and Lud, and Aram, and Hus, and Hul, and Gether, and Mosoch.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	18	And Arphaxad beget Sale, and Sale beget Heber.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	19	And to Heber were born two sons, the name of the one was Phaleg, because In his days the earth was divided; and the name of his brother was Jectan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	20	And Jectan beget Elmodad, and Saleph, and Asarmoth, and Jare,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	21	And Adoram, and Usal, and Decla,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	22	And Hebal, and Abimael, and Saba,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	23	And Ophir, and Hevila, and Jobab. All these are the sons of Jectan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	24	Sem, Arphaxad, Sale,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	25	Heber, Phaleg, Ragau,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	26	Serug, Nachor, Thare,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	27	Abram, this is Abraham.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	28	And the sons of Abraham, Isaac and Ismahel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	29	And these are the generations of them. The firstborn of Ismahel, Nabajoth, then Cedar, and Adbeel, and Mabsam,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	30	And Masma, and Duma, Massa, Hadad, and Thema,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	31	Jetur, Naphis, Cedma: these are the sons of Ismahel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	32	And the sons of Cetura, Abraham's concubine, whom she bore: Zamran, Jecsan, Madan, Madian, Jesboc, and Sue. And the sons of Jecsan, Saba, and Dadan. And the sons of Dadan: Assurim, and Latussim, and Laomin.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	33	And the sons of Madian: Epha, and Epher, and Henoch, and Abida, and Eldaa. All these are the sons of Cetura.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	34	And Abraham beget Isaac: and his sons were Esau and Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	35	The sons of Esau: Eliphaz, Rahuel, Jehus, Ihelom, and Core.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	36	The sons of Eliphaz: Theman, Omar, Sephi, Gathan, Cenez, and by Thamna, Amalec.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	37	The sons of Rahuel: Nahath, Zara, Samma, Meza.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	38	The sons of Seir: Lotan. Sobal, Sebeen, Ana, Dison, Eser, Disan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	39	The sons of Lotan: Hori, Homam. And the sister of Lotan was Thamna.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	40	The sons of Sobal: Alian, and Manahath, and Ebal, Sephi and Onam. The sons of Sebeon: Aia, and Ana. The son of Ana: Dison.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	41	The sons of Dison: Hamram, and Eseban, and Jethran, and Charan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	42	The sons of Eser: Balaan, and Zavan, and Jacan. The sons of Disan: Hus and Aran.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	43	Now these are the kings that reigned in the land of Edom, before there was a king over the children of Israel: Bale the son of Beer: and the name of his city was Denaba.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	44	And Bale died, and Jobab the son of Zare of Bosra, reigned in his stead.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	45	And when Jobab also was dead, Husam of the land of the Themanites reigned in his stead.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	46	And Husam also died, and Adad the son of Badad reigned in his stead, and he defeated the Madianites in the land of Moab: and the name of his city was Avith.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	47	And when Adad also was dead, Semla of Masreca reigned in his stead.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	48	Semla also died, and Saul of Rohoboth, which is near the river, reigned in his stead.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	49	And when Saul was dead, Balanan the son of Achobor reigned in his stead.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	50	He also died, and Adad reigned in his stead: and the name of his city was Phau, and his wife was called Meetabel the daughter of Matred, the daughter of Mezaab.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	51	And after the death of Adad, there began to be dukes in Edom instead of kings: duke Thamna, duke Alva, duke Jetheth,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	52	Duke Oolibama, duke Ela, duke Phinon,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	53	Duke Cenez, duke Theman, duke Mabsar,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	1	54	Duke Magdiel, duke Hiram. These are the dukes of Edom.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	1	And these are the sons of Israel: Ruben, Simeon, Levi, Juda, Issachar, and Zabulon,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	2	Dan, Joseph, Benjamin, Nephtali, Gad, and Aser.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	3	The sons of Juda: Her, Onan and Sela. These three were born to him of the Chanaanitess the daughter of Sue. And Her the firstborn of Juda, was wicked in the sight of the Lord, and he slew him.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	4	And Thamar his daughter in law bore him Phares and Zara. So all the sons of Juda were five.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	5	And the sons of Phares, were Hesron and Hamul.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	6	And the sons also of Zare: Zamri, and Ethan, and Eman, and Chalchal, and Dara, five in all.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	7	And the sons of Charmi: Achar, who troubled Israel, and sinned by the theft of the anathema.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	8	The sons of Ethan: Azarias,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	9	And the sons of Hesron that were born to him: Jerameel, and Ram, and Calubi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	10	And Ram beget Aminadab, and Aminadab beget Nahasson, prince of the children of Juda.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	11	And Nahasson beget Salma, the father of Booz.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	12	And Booz beget Obed, and Obed beget Isai.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	13	And Isai beget Eliab his firstborn, the second Abinadab, the third Simmaa,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	14	The fourth, Nathanael, the fifth Raddai,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	15	The sixth Asom, the seventh David.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	16	And their sisters were Sarvia, and Abigail. The sons of Sarvia: Abisai, Joab, and Asael, three.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	17	And Abigail bore Amasa, whose father was Jether the Ismahelite.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	18	And Caleb the son of Hesron took a wife named Azuba, of whom he had Jerioth: and her sons were Jaser, and Sobab, and Ardon.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	19	And when Azuba was dead, Caleb took to wife Ephrata: who bore him Hur.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	20	And Hur beget Uri: and Uri beget Bezeleel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	21	And afterwards Hesron went in to the daughter of Machir the father of Galaad, and took her to wife when he was threescore years old: and she bore him Segub.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	22	And Segub beget Jair, and he had three and twenty cities in the land of Galaad.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	23	And he took Gessur, and Aram the towns of Jair, and Canath, and the villages thereof, threescore cities. All these, the sons of Machir father of Galaad.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	24	And when Hesron was dead, Caleb went in to Ephrata. Hesron also had to wife Abia who bore him Ashur the father of Thecua.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	25	And the sons of Jerameel the firstborn of Hesron, were Ram his firstborn, and Buna, and Aram, and Asom, and Achia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	26	And Jerameel married another wife, named Atara, who was the mother of Onam.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	27	And the sons of Ram the firstborn of Jerameel, were Moos, Jamin, and Achar.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	28	And Onam had sons Semei, and Jada. And the sons of Semei: Nadab, and Abisur.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	29	And the name of Abisur's wife was Abihail, who bore him Ahobban, and Molid.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	30	And the sons of Nadab were Saled, and Apphaim. And Saled died without children.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	31	But the son of Apphaim was Jesi: and Jesi beget Sesan. And Sesan beget Oholai.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	32	And the sons of Jada the brother of Semei: Jether and Jonathan. And Jether also died without children.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	33	But Jonathan beget Phaleth, and Ziza, These were the sons of Jerameel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	34	And Sesan had no sons, but daughters and a servant an Egyptian, named Jeraa.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	35	And he gave him his daughter to wife: and she bore him Ethei.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	36	And Ethei begot Nathan, and Nathan beget Zabad.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	37	And Zabad beget Ophlal, and Ophlal beget Obed.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	38	Obed beget Jehu, Jehu beget Azarias.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	39	Azarias beget Helles, and Helles begot Elasa.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	40	Elasa beget Sisamoi, Sisamoi beget Sellum,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	41	Sellum beget Icamia, and Icamia begot Elisama.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	42	Now the sons of Caleb the brother of Jerameel were Mesa his firstborn, who was the father of Siph: and the sons of Maresa father of Hebron.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	43	And the sons of Hebron, Core, and Thaphua, and Recem, and Samma.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	44	And Samma beget Raham, the father of Jercaam, and Recem beget Sammai.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	45	The son of Sammai, Maon: and Maon the father of Bethsur.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	46	And Epha the concubine of Caleb bore Haran, and Mesa, and Gezez. And Haran beget Gezez.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	47	And the sons of Jahaddai, Rogom, and Joathan, and Gesan, and Phalet, and Epha, and Saaph.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	48	And Maacha the concubine of Caleb bore Saber, and Tharana.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	49	And Saaph the father of Madmena beget Sue the father of Machbena, and the father of Gabaa. And the daughter of Caleb was Achsa.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	50	These were the sons of Caleb, the son of Hur the firstborn of Ephrata, Sobal the father of Cariathiarim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	51	Salma the father of Bethlehem, Hariph the father of Bethgader.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	52	And Sobal the father of Cariathiarim had sons: he that saw half of the places of rest.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	53	And of the kindred of Cariathiarim, the Jethrites, and Aphuthites, and Semathites, and Maserites. Of them came the Saraites, and Esthaolites.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	54	The sons of Salma, Bethlehem, and Netophathi, the crowns of the house of Joab, and half of the place of rest of Sarai.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	2	55	And the families of the scribes that dwell in Jabes, singing and making melody, and abiding in tents. These are the Cinites, who came of Calor (Chamath) father of the house of Rechab,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	1	Now these were the sons of David that were born to him in Hebron: the firstborn Amnon of Achinoam the Jezrahelitess, the second Daniel of Abigail the Carmelitess.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	2	The third Absalom the son of Maacha the daughter of Tolmai king of Gessur, the fourth Adonias the son of Aggith,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	3	The fifth Saphatias of Abital, the sixth Jethrahem of Egla, his wife.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	4	So six sons were born to him in Hebron, where he reigned seven years and six months. And in Jerusalem he reigned three and thirty years.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	5	And these sons were born to him in Jerusalem: Simmaa, and Sobab, and Nathan, and Solomon, four of Bethsabee the daughter of Ammiel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	6	Jebaar also and Elisama,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	7	And Eliphaleeh, and Noge, and Nepheg, and Japhia,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	8	And Elisama, and Eliada, and Elipheleth, nine:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	9	All these the sons of David, beside the sons of the concubines: and they had a sister Thamar.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	10	And Solomon's son was Roboam: whose son Abia beget Asa. And his son was Josaphat,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	11	The father of Joram: and Joram begot Ochozias, of whom was born Joas:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	12	And his son Amasias begot Azarias. And Joathan the son of Azarias
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	13	Beget Achaz, the father of Ezechias, of whom was born Manasses.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	14	And Manasses beget Amen the father of Josias.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	15	And the sons of Josias were, the firstborn Johanan, the second Joakim, the third Sedecias, the fourth Sellum.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	16	Of Joakim was born Jechonias, and Sedecias.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	17	The sons of Jechonias were Asir, Salathiel,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	18	Melchiram, Phadaia, Senneser and Jecemia, Sama, and Nadabia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	19	Of Phadaia were born Zorobabel and Semei. Zorobabel beget Mosollam, Hananias, and Salomith their sister:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	20	Hasaba also, and Ohol, and Barachias, and Hasadias, Josabhesed, five.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	21	And the son of Hananias was Phaltias the father of Jeseias, whose son was Raphaia. And his son was Arnan, of whom was born Obdia, whose son was Sechenias.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	22	The son of Sechenias, was Semeia, whose sons were Hattus, and Jegaal, and Baria, and Naaria, and Saphat, six in number.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	23	The sons of Naaria, Elioenai, and Ezechias, and Ezricam, three.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	3	24	The sons of Elioenai, Oduia, and Eliasub, and Pheleia, and Accub, and Johanan, and Dalaia, and Anani, seven.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	1	The sons of Juda: Phares, Hesron, and Charmi, and Hur, and Sobal.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	2	And Raia the son of Sobal beget Jahath, of whom were born Ahumai, and Laad. These are the families of Sarathi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	3	And this is the posterity of Etam: Jezrahel, and Jesema, and Jedebos: and the name of their sister was Asalelphuni.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	4	And Phanuel the father of Gedor, and Ezar the father of Hosa, these are the sons of Hur the firstborn of Ephratha the father of Bethlehem.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	5	And Assur the father of Thecua had two wives, Halaa and Naara:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	6	And Naara bore him Ozam, and Hepher, and Themani, and Ahasthari: these are the sons of Naara.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	7	And the sons of Halaa, Sereth, Isaar, and Ethnan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	8	And Cos begot Anob, and Soboba, the kindred of Aharehel the son of Arum.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	9	And Jabes was more honourable than any of his brethren, and his mother called his name Jabes, saying: Because I bore him with sorrow.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	10	And Jabes called upon the God of Israel, saying: If blessing thou wilt bless me, and wilt enlarge my borders, and thy hand be with me, and thou save me from being oppressed by evil. And God granted him the things he prayed for.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	11	And Caleb the brother of Sua beget Mahir, who was the father of Esthon.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	12	And Esthon beget Bethrapha, and Phesse, and Tehinna father of the city of Naas: these are the men of Recha.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	13	And the sons of Cenez were Othoniel, and Saraia. And the sons of Othoniel, Hathath, and Maonathi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	14	Maonathi beget Ophra, and Saraia begot Joab the father of the Valley of artificers: for artificers were there.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	15	And the sons of Caleb the son of Jephone, were Hir, and Ela, and Naham. And the sons of Ela: Cenez.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	16	The sons also of Jaleleel: Ziph, and Zipha, Thiria, and Asrael.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	17	And the sons of Esra, Jether, and Mered, and Epher, and Jalon, and he beget Mariam, and Sammai, and Jesba the father of Esthamo.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	18	And his wife Judaia, bore Jared the father of Gedor, and Heber the father of Socho, and Icuthiel the father of Zanoe. And these are the sons of Bethia the daughter of Pharao, whom Mered took to wife.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	19	And the sons of his wife Odaia the sister of Naham the father of Celia, Garmi, and Esthamo, who was of Machathi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	20	The sons also of Simon, Amnon, and Rinna the son of Hanan, and Thilon. And the sons of Jesi Zoheth, and Benzoheth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	21	The sons of Sela the son of Juda: Her the father of Lecha, and Laada the father of Maresa, and the families of the house of them that wrought fine linen in the House of oath.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	22	And he that made the sun to stand, and the men of Lying, and Secure, and Burning, who were princes in Moab, and who returned into Lahem. Now these are things of old.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	23	These are the potters, and they dwelt in Plantations, and Hedges, with the king for his works, and they abode there.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	24	The sons of Simeon: Namuel, and Jamin, Jarib, Zara, Saul:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	25	Sellum his son, Mapsam his son, Masma his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	26	The sons of Masma: Hamuel his son, Zachur his son, Semei his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	27	The sons of Semei were sixteen, and six daughters: but his brethren had not many sons, and the whole kindred could not reach to the sum of the children of Juda.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	28	And they dwelt in Bersabee, and Molada, and Hasarsuhal,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	29	And in Bala, and in Asom, and in Tholad,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	30	And in Bathuel, and in Horma, and in Siceleg,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	31	And in Bethmarchaboth, and in Hasarsusim, and in Bethberai, and in Saarim. These were their cities unto the reign of David.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	32	Their towns also were Etam, and Aen, Remmon, and Thochen, and Asan, five cities.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	33	And all their villages round about these cities as far as Baal. This was their habitation, and the distribution of their dwellings.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	34	And Mosabab and Jemlech, and Josa, the son of Amasias,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	35	And Joel, and Jehu the son of Josabia the son of Saraia, the son of Asiel,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	36	And Elioenai, and Jacoba, and Isuhaia, and Asaia, and Adiel, and Ismiel, and Banaia,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	37	Ziza also the son of Sephei the son of Allon the son of Idaia the son of Semri the son of Samaia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	38	These were named princes in their kindreds, and in the houses of their families were multiplied exceedingly.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	39	And they went forth to enter into Gador as far as to the east side of the valley, to seek pastures for their flocks.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	40	And they found fat pastures, and very good, and a country spacious, and quiet, and fruitful, in which some of the race of Cham had dwelt before.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	41	And these whose names are written above, came in the days of Ezechias king of Juda: and they beat down their tents, and slew the inhabitants that were found there, and utterly destroyed them unto this day: and they dwelt in their place, because they found there fat pastures.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	42	Some also of the children of Simeon, five hundred men, went into mount Seir, having for their captains Phaltias and Naaria and Raphaia and Oziel the sons of Jesi:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	4	43	And they slew the remnant of the Amalecites, who had been able to escape, and they dwelt there in their stead unto this day.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	1	Now the sons of Ruben the firstborn of Israel, (for he was his firstborn: but forasmuch as he defiled his father's bed, his first birthright was given to the sons of Joseph the son of Israel, and he was not accounted for the firstborn.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	2	But of the race of Juda, who was the strongest among his brethren, came the princes: but the first birthright was accounted to Joseph.)
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	3	The sons then of Ruben the firstborn of Israel were Enoch, and Phallu, Esron, and Charmi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	4	The sons of Joel: Samaia his son, Gog his son, Semei his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	5	Micha his son, Reia his son, Baal his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	6	Beera his son, whom Thelgathphalnasar king of the Assyrians carried away captive, and he was prince in the tribe of Ruben.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	7	And his brethren, and all his kindred, when they were numbered by their families, had for princes Jehiel, and Zacharias.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	8	And Bala the son of Azaz, the son of Samma, the son of Joel, dwelt in Aroer as far as Nebo, and Beelmeon.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	9	And eastward he had his habitation as far as the entrance of the desert, and the river Euphrates. For they possessed a great number of cattle in the land of Galaad.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	10	And in the days of Saul they fought against the Agarites, and slew them, and dwelt in their tents in their stead, in all the country, that looketh to the east of Galaad.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	11	And the children of Gad dwelt over against them in the land of Basan, as far as Selcha:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	12	Johel the chief, and Saphan the second: and Janai, and Saphat in Basan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	13	And their brethren according to the houses of their kindreds, were Michael, and Mosollam, and Sebe, and Jorai, and Jacan, and Zie, and Heber, seven.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	14	These were the sons of Abihail, the son of Hurl, the son of Jara, the son of Galaad, the son of Michael, the son of Jesisi, the son of Jeddo, the son of But.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	15	And their brethren the sons of Abdiel, the son of Guni, chief of the house in their families,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	16	And they dwelt in Galaad, and in Basan and in the towns thereof, and in all the suburbs of Saron, unto the borders.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	17	All these were numbered in the days of Joathan king of Juda, and in the days of Jeroboam king of Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	18	The sons of Ruben, and of Gad, and of the half tribe of Manasses, fighting men, bearing shields, and swords, and bending the bow, and trained up to battles, four and forty thousand seven hundred and threescore that went out to war.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	19	They fought against the Agarites: but the Itureans, and Naphis, and Nodab,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	20	Gave them help. And the Agarites were delivered into their hands, and all that were with them, because they called upon God in the battle: and he heard them, because they had put their faith in him.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	21	And they took all that they possessed, of camels fifty thousand, and of sheep two hundred and fifty thousand, and of asses two thousand, and of men a hundred thousand souls.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	22	And many fell down slain: for it was the battle of the Lord. And they dwelt in their stead till the captivity.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	23	And the children of the half tribe of Manasses possessed the land, from the borders of Basan unto Baal, Hermon, and Sanir, and mount Hermon, for their number was great.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	24	And these were the heads of the house of their kindred, Epher, and Jesi, and Eliel, and Esriel, and Jeremia, and Odoia, and Jediel, most valiant and powerful men, and famous chiefs in their families.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	25	But they forsook the God of their fathers, and went astray after the gods of the people of the land, whom God destroyed before them.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	5	26	And the God of Israel stirred up the spirit of Phul king of the Assyrians, and the spirit of Thelgathphalnasar king of Assur: and he carried away Ruben, and Gad, and the half tribe of Manasses, and brought them to Lahela, and to Habor, and to Ara, and to the river of Gozan, unto this day.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	1	The sons of Levi were Gerson, Caath, and Merari.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	2	The sons of Caath: Amram, Isaar, Hebron, and Oziel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	3	The children of Amram: Aaron, Moses, and Mary. The sons of Aaron: Nadab and Abiu, Eleazar and Ithamar.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	4	Eleazar beget Phinees, and Phinees beget Abisue,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	5	And Abisue beget Bocci, and Bocci begot Ozi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	6	Ozi beget Zaraias, and Zaraias beget Maraioth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	7	And Maraioth beget Amarias, and Amarias beget Achitob.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	8	Achitob beget Sadoc, and Sadoc begot Achimaas.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	9	Achimaas beget Azarias, Azarias begot Johanan,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	10	Johanan beget Azarias. This is he that executed the priestly office in the house which Solomon built in Jerusalem.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	11	And Azarias beget Amarias, and Amarias beget Achitob.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	12	And Achitob beget Sadoc, and Sadoc beget Sellum,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	13	Sellum beget Helcias, and Helcias beget Azarias,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	14	Azarias beget Saraias, and Saraias beget Josedec.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	15	Now Josedec went out, when the Lord carried away Juda, and Jerusalem, by the hands of Nabuchodonosor.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	16	So the sons of Levi were Gerson, Caath, and Merari.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	17	And these are the names of the sons of Gerson: Lobni and Semei.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	18	The sons of Caath: Amram, and Isaar, and Hebron, and Oziel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	19	The sons of Merari: Moholi and Musi. And these are the kindreds of Levi according to their families.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	20	Of Gerson: Lobni his son, Jahath his son, Zamma his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	21	Joah his son, Addo his son, Zara his son, Jethrai his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	22	The sons of Caath, Aminadab his son, Core his son, Asir his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	23	Elcana his son, Abiasaph his son, Asir his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	24	Thahath his son, Uriel his son, Ozias his son, Saul his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	25	The sons of Elcana: Amasai, and Achimoth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	26	And Elcana. The sons of Elcana: Sophai his son, Nahath his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	27	Eliab his son, Jeroham his son, Elcana his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	28	The sons of Samuel: the firstborn Vasseni, and Abia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	29	And the sons of Merari, Moholi: Lobni his son, Semei his son, Oza his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	30	Sammaa his son, Haggia his son, Asaia his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	31	These are they, whom David set over the singing men of the house of the Lord, after that the ark was placed:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	32	And they ministered before the tabernacle of the testimony, with singing, until Solomon built the house of the Lord in Jerusalem, and they stood according to their order in the ministry.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	33	And these are they that stood with their sons, of the sons of Caath, Hemam a singer, the son of Joel, the son of Sammuel,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	34	The son of Elcana, the son of Jeroham, the son of Eliel, the son of Thohu,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	35	The son of Suph, the son of Elcana, the son of Mahath, the son of Amasai,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	36	The son of Elcana, the son of Johel, the son of Azarias, the son of Sophonias,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	37	The son of Thahath, the son of Asir, the son or Abiasaph, the son of Core,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	38	The son of Isaar, the son of Caath, the son of Levi, the son of Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	39	And his brother Asaph, who stood on his right hand, Asaph the son of Barachias, the son of Samaa.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	40	The son of Michael, the son of Basaia, the son of Melchia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	41	The son of Athanai, the son of Zara, the son of Adaia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	42	The son of Ethan, the son of Zamma, the son of Semei.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	43	The son of Jeth, the son of Gerson, the son of Levi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	44	And the sons of Merari their brethren, on the left hand, Ethan the son of Cusi, the son of Abdi, the son of Meloch,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	45	The son of Hasabia, the son of Amasai, the son of Helcias,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	46	The son of Amasai, the son of Boni, the son of Somer,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	47	The son of Moholi, the son of Mud, the son of Merari, the son of Levi.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	48	Their brethren also the Levites, who were appointed for all the ministry of the tabernacle of the house of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	49	But Aaron and his sons offered burnt offerings upon the altar of holocausts, and upon the altar of incense, for very work of the holy of holies: and to pray for Israel according to all that Moses the servant of God had commanded.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	50	And these are the sons of Aaron: Eleazar his son, Phinees his son, Abisue his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	51	Bocci his son, Ozi his son, Zarahia his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	52	Meraioth his son, Amarias his son, Achitob his son,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	53	Sadoc his son, Achimaas his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	54	And these are their dwelling places by the towns and confines, to wit, of the sons of Aaron, of the families of the Caathites: for they fell to them by lot.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	55	And they gave them Hebron in the land of Juda, and the suburbs thereof round about:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	56	But the fields of the city, and the villages to Caleb son of Jephone.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	57	And to the sons of Aaron they gave the cities for refuge Hebron, and Lobna, and the suburbs thereof,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	58	And Jether and Esthemo, with their suburbs, and Helon, and Dabir with their suburbs:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	59	Asan also, and Bethsames, with their suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	60	And out of the tribe of Benjamin: Gabee and its suburbs, Almath with its suburbs, Anathoth also with its suburbs: all their cities throughout their families were thirteen.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	61	And to the sons of Caath that remained of their kindred they gave out of the half tribe of Manasses ten cities in possession.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	62	And to the sons of Gerson by their families out of the tribe of Issachar, and out of the tribe of Aser, and out of the tribe of Nephtali, and out of the tribe of Manasses in Basan, thirteen cities.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	63	And to the sons of Merari by their families out of the tribe of Ruben, and out of the tribe of Gad, and out of the tribe of Zabulon, they gave by lot twelve cities.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	64	And the children of Israel gave to the Levites the cities, and their suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	65	And they gave them by lot, out of the tribe of the sons of Juda, and out of the tribe of the sons of Simeon, and out of the tribe of the sons of Benjamin, these cities which they called by their names.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	66	And to them that were of the kindred of the sons of Caath, and the cities in their borders were of the tribe of Ephraim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	67	And they gave the cities of refuge Sichem with its suburbs in mount Ephraim, and Gazer with its suburbs,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	68	Jecmaan also with its suburbs, and Beth-horon in like manner,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	69	Helon also with its suburbs, and Gethremmon in like manner,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	70	And out of the half tribe of Manasses, Aner and its suburbs, Baalam and its suburbs: to wit, to them that were left of the family of the sons of Caath.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	71	And to the sons of Gersom, out of the kindred of the half tribe of Manasses, Gaulon, in Basan, and its suburbs, and Astharoth with its suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	72	Out of the tribe of Issachar, Cedes and its suburbs, and Dabereth with its suburbs;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	73	Ramoth also and its suburbs, and Anem with its suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	74	And out of the tribe of Aser: Masal with its suburbs, and Abdon in like manner;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	75	Hucac also and its suburbs, and Rohol with its suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	76	And out of the tribe of Nephtali, Cedes in Galilee and its suburbs, Hamon with its suburbs, and Cariathaim, and its suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	77	And to the sons of Merari that remained: out of the tribe of Zabulon, Remmono and its suburbs, and Thabor with its suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	78	Beyond the Jordan also over against Jericho, on the east side of the Jordan, out of the tribe of Ruben, Bosor in the wilderness with its suburbs, and Jassa with its suburbs;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	79	Cademoth also and its suburbs, and Mephaath with its suburbs;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	80	Moreover also out of the tribe of Gad, Ramoth in Galaad and its suburbs, and Manaim with its suburbs;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	6	81	Hesebon also with its suburbs, and Jazer with its suburbs.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	1	Now the sons of Issachar were Thola, and Phua, Jasub and Simeron, four.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	2	The sons of Thola: Ozi and Raphaia, and Jeriel, and Jemai, and Jebsem, and Samuel, chiefs of the houses of their kindreds. Of the posterity of Thola were numbered in the days of David, two and twenty thousand six hundred most valiant men.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	3	The sons of Ozi: Izrahia, of whom were born Michael, and Obadia, and Joel, and Jesia, five all great men.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	4	And there were with them by their families and peoples, six and thirty thousand most valiant men ready for war: for they had many wives and children.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	5	Their brethren also throughout all the house of Issachar, were numbered fourscore and seven thousand most valiant men for war.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	6	The sons of Benjamin were Bela, and Bechor, and Jadihel, three.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	7	The sons of Bela: Esbon, and Ozi, and Ozial, and Jerimoth and Urai, five chiefs of their families, and most valiant warriors, and their number was twenty-two thousand and thirty-four.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	8	And the sons of Bechor were Zamira, and Joas, and Eliezer, and Elioenai, and Amai, and Jerimoth, and Abia, and Anathoth, and Almath: all these were the sons of Bechor.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	9	And they were numbered by the families, heads of their kindreds, most valiant men for war, twenty thousand and two hundred.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	10	And the son of Jadihel: Balan. And the sons of Balan: Jehus and Benjamin and Aod, and Chanana, and Zethan and Tharsis, and Ahisahar.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	11	All these were sons of Jadihel, heads of their kindreds, most valiant men, seventeen thousand and two hundred fit to go out to war.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	12	Sepham also and Hapham the sons of Hir: and Hasim the sons of Aher.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	13	And the sons of Nephtali were Jasiel, and Guni, and Jezer, and Sellum, sons of Bala.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	14	And the son of Manasses, Ezriel: and his concubine the Syrian bore Machir the father of Galaad.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	15	And Machir took wives for his sons Happhim, and Saphan: and he had a sister named Maacha: the name of the second was Salphaad, and Salphaad had daughters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	16	And Maacha the wife of Machir bore a son, and she called his name Phares: and the name of his brother was Sares: and his sons were Ulam and Recen.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	17	And the son of Ulam, Baden. These are the sons of Galaad, the son of Machir the son of Manasses.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	18	And his sister named Queen bore Goodlyman, and Abiezer, and Mohola.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	19	And the sons of Semida were Ahiu, and Sechem, and Leci and Aniam.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	20	And the sons of Ephraim were Suthala, Bared his son, Thahath his son, Elada his son, Thahath his son, and his son Zabad,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	21	And his son Suthala, and his son Ezer, and Elad: and the men of Geth born in the land slew them, because they came down to invade their possessions.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	22	And Ephraim their father mourned many days, and his brethren came to comfort him.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	23	And he went in to his wife: and she conceived and bore a son, and he called his name Beria, because he was born when it went evil with his house:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	24	And his daughter was Sara, who built Bethoron, the nether and the upper, and Ozensara.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	25	And Rapha was his son, and Reseph, and Thale, of whom was born Thaan,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	26	Who begot Laadan: and his son was Ammiud, who beget Elisama,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	27	Of whom was born Nun, who had Josue for his son.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	28	And their possessions and habitations were Bethel with her daughters, and eastward Noran, and westward Gazer and her daughters, Sichem also with her daughters, as far as Ass with her daughters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	29	And by the borders of the sons of Manasses Bethsan and her daughters, Thanach and her daughters, Mageddo and her daughters: Dor and her daughters: in these dwelt the children of Joseph, the son of Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	30	The children of Aser were Jemna, and Jesua, and Jessui, and Baria, and Sara their sister.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	31	And the sons of Baria: Haber, and Melchiel: he is the father of Barsaith.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	32	And Heber beget Jephlat, and Somer, and Hotham, and Suaa their sister.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	33	The sons of Jephlat: Phosech, and Chamaal, and Asoth: these are the sons of Jephlat.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	34	And the sons of Somer: Ahi, and Roaga, and Haba, and Aram.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	35	And the sons of Helem his brother: Supha, and Jemna, and Selles, and Amal.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	36	The sons of Supha: Sue, Hernapher, and Sual, and Beri, and Jamra.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	37	Bosor and Hod, and Samma, and Salusa, and Jethran, and Bera.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	38	The sons of Jether: Jephone, and Phaspha, and Ara.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	39	And the sons of Olla: Aree, and Haniel, and Resia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	7	40	All these were sons of Aser, heads of their families, choice and most valiant captains of captains: and the number of them that were of the age that was fit for war, was six and twenty thousand.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	1	Now Benjamin beget Bale his firstborn, Asbel the second, Ahara the third,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	2	Nohaa the fourth, and Rapha the fifth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	3	And the sons of Bale were Addar, and Gera, and Abiud,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	4	And Abisue, and Naamar, and Ahoe,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	5	And Gera, and Sephuphan, and Huram.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	6	These are the sons of Ahod, heads of families that dwelt in Gabaa, who were removed into Mrtnahsth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	7	And Naaman, and Achia, and Gera he removed them, and beget Oza, and Ahiud.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	8	And Saharim begot in the land of Moab, after he sent away Husim and Bara his wives.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	9	And he beget of Hodes his wife Jobab, and Sebia, and Mesa, and Molchom,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	10	And Jehus and Sechia, and Marma. These were his sons heads of their families.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	11	And Mehusim beget Abitob, and Elphaal.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	12	And the sons of Elphaal were Heber, and Misaam, and Samad: who built One, and Led, and its daughters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	13	And Baria, and Sama were heads of their kindreds that dwelt in Aialon: these drove away the inhabitants of Geth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	14	And Ahio, and Sesac, and Jerimoth,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	15	And Zabadia, and Arod, and Heder,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	16	And Michael, and Jespha, and Joha, the sons of Baria.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	17	And Zabadia, and Mosollam, and Hezeci, and Heber,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	18	And Jesamari, and Jezlia, and Jobab, sons of Elphaal,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	19	And Jacim, and Zechri, and Zabdi,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	20	And Elioenai, and Selethai, and Elial,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	21	And Adaia, and Baraia, and Samareth, the sons of Semei.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	22	And Jespham, and Heber, and Eliel,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	23	And Abdon, and Zechri, and Hanan,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	24	And Hanania, and Elam, and Anathothia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	25	And Jephdaia, and Phanuel the sons of Sesac.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	26	And Samsari, and Sohoria and Otholia,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	27	And Jersia, and Elia, and Zechri, the sons of Jeroham.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	28	These were the chief fathers, and heads of their families who dwelt in Jerusalem.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	29	And at Gabaon dwelt Abigabaon, and the name of his wife was Maacha:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	30	And his firstborn son Abdon, and Sur, and Cia, and Baal, and Nadab,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	31	And Gedor, and Ahio, and Zacher, and Macelloth:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	32	And Macelloth beget Samaa: and they dwelt over against their brethren in Jerusalem with their brethren.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	33	And Ner beget Cia, and Cia beget Saul. And Saul begot Jonathan and Melchisua, and Abinadab, and Esbaal.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	34	And the son of Jonathan was Meribbaal: and Meribbaal begot Micha.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	35	And the sons of Micha were Phithon, and Melech, and Tharaa, and Ahaz.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	36	And Ahaz beget Joada: and Joada beget Alamath, and Azmoth, and Zamri: and Zamri beget Mesa,
