1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	38	And Asel had six sons whose names were Ezricam, Bochru, Ismahel, Saria, Obdia, and Hanan. All these were the sons of Asel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	39	And the sons of Esec, his brother, were Ulam the firstborn, and Jehus the second, and Eliphelet the third.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	8	40	And the sons of Ulam were most valiant men, and archers of great strength: and they had many sons and grandsons, even to a hundred and fifty. All these were children of Benjamin.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	1	And all Israel was numbered: and the sum of them was written in the book of the kings of Israel, and Juda: and they were carried away to Babylon for their transgression.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	2	Now the first that dwelt in their possessions, and in their cities, were the Israelites, and the priests, and the Levites, and the Nathineans.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	3	And in Jerusalem dwelt of the children of Juda, and of the children of Benjamin, and of the children of Ephraim, and of Manasses.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	4	Othei the son of Ammiud, the son of Amri, the son of Omrai, the son of Bonni, of the sons of Phares the son of Juda.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	5	And of Siloni: Asaia the firstborn, and his sons.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	6	And of the sons of Zara: Jehuel, and their brethren, six hundred and ninety.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	7	And of the sons of Benjamin: Sale the son of Mosollam, the son of Oduia, the son of Asana:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	8	And Jobania the son of Jeroham: and Ela the son of Ozi, the son of Mochori: and Mosallam the son of Saphatias, the son of Rahuel, the son of Jebania:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	9	And their brethren by their families, nine hundred and fifty-six. All these were heads of their families, by the houses of their fathers.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	10	And of the priests: Jedaia, Joiarib, and Jachin:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	11	And Azarias the son of Helcias, the son of Mosollam, the son of Sadoc, the son of Maraioth, the son of Achitob, high priest of the house of God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	12	And Adaias the son of Jeroham, the son of Phassur, the son of Melchias, and Maasai the son of Adiel, the son of Jezra, the son of Mosollam, the son of Mosollamith, the son of Emmer.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	13	And their brethren heads in their families a thousand seven hundred and threescore, very strong and able men for the work of the ministry in the house of God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	14	And of the Levites: Semeia the son of Hassub the son of Ezricam, the son of Hasebia of the sons of Merari.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	15	And Bacbacar the carpenter, and Galal, and Mathania the son of Micha, the son of Zechri the son of Asaph:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	16	And Obdia the son of Semeia, the son of Galal, the son of Idithum: and Barachia the son of Asa, the son of Elcana, who dwelt in the suburbs of Netophati.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	17	And the porters were Sellum, and Accub, and Telmon, and Ahiman: and their brother Sellum was the prince,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	18	Until that time, in the king's gate eastward, the sons of Levi waited by their turns.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	19	But Sellum the son of Core, the son of Abiasaph, the son of Core, with his brethren and his father's house, the Corites were over the works of the service, keepers of the gates of the tabernacle: and their families in turns were keepers of the entrance of the camp of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	20	And Phinees the son of Eleazar, was their prince before the Lord,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	21	And Zacharias the son of Mosollamia, was porter of the gate of the tabernacle of the testimony:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	22	All these that were chosen to be porters at the gates, were two hundred and twelve: and they were registered in their proper towns: whom David and Samuel the seer appointed in their trust.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	23	As well them as their sons, to keep the gates of the house of the Lord, and the tabernacle by their turns.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	24	In four quarters were the porters: that is to say, toward the east, and west, and north, and south.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	25	And their brethren dwelt in villages, and came upon their sabbath days from time to time.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	26	To these four Levites were committed the whole number of the porters, and they were over the chambers, and treasures, of the house of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	27	And they abode in their watches round about the temple of the Lord: that when it was time, they might open the gates in the morning.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	28	And some of their stock had the charge of the vessels for the ministry: for the vessels were both brought in and carried out by number.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	29	Some of them also had the instruments of the sanctuary committed unto them, and the charge of the fine flour, and wine, and oil, and frankincense, and spices.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	30	And the sons of the priests made the ointments of the spices.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	31	And Mathathias a Levite, the firstborn of Sellum the Corite, was overseer of such things as were fried in the fryingpan.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	32	And some of the sons of Caath their brethren, were over the loaves of proposition, to prepare always new for every sabbath.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	33	These are the chief of the singing men of the families of the Levites, who dwelt in the chambers, by the temple, that they might serve continually day and night in their ministry.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	34	The heads of the Levites, princes in their families, abode in Jerusalem.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	35	And in Gabaon dwelt Jehiel the father of Gabaon, and the name of hill wife was Maacha:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	36	His firstborn son Abdon, and Sur, and Cis, and Baal, and Ner, and Nadab,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	37	Gedor also, and Ahio, and Zacharias, and Macelloth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	38	And Macelloth beget Samaan: these dwelt over against their brethren in Jerusalem, with their brethren.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	9	39	Now Ner beget Cia: and Cis begot Saul: and Saul beget Jonathan and Melchisua, and Abinadab, and Esbaal.
