1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	1	Now these are they that came to David to Siceleg, while he yet fled from Saul the son of Cis, and they were most valiant and excellent warriors,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	2	Bending the bow, and using either hand in hurling stones with slings, and shooting arrows: of the brethren of Saul of Benjamin.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	3	The chief was Ahiezer, and Joas, the sons of Samaa of Gabaath, and Jaziel, and Phallet the sons of Azmoth, and Beracha, and Jehu an Anathothite.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	4	And Samaias of Gabaon, the stoutest amongst the thirty and over the thirty; Jeremias, and Jeheziel, and Johanan, and Jezabad of Gaderoth;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	5	And Eluzai, and Jerimuth, and Baalia, and Samaria, and Saphatia the Haruphite;
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	6	Elcana, and Jesia, and Azareel, and Joezer, and Jesbaam of Carehim:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	7	And Joela, and Zabadia the sons of Jeroham of Gedor.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	8	From Gaddi also there went over to David, when he lay hid in the wilderness most valiant men, and excellent warriors, holding shield and spear: whose faces were like the faces of a lion, and they were swift like the roebucks on the mountains.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	9	Ezer the chief, Obdias the second, Eliab the third,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	10	Masmana the fourth, Jeremias the fifth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	11	Ethi the sixth, Eliel the seventh,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	12	Johanan the eighth, Elzebad the ninth,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	13	Jerenias the tenth, Machbani the eleventh,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	14	These were of the sons of Gad, captains of the army: the least of them was captain over a hundred soldiers, and the greatest over a thousand.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	15	These are they who passed over the Jordan in the first month, when it is used to how over its banks: and they put to flight all that dwelt in the valleys both toward the east and toward the west.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	16	And there came also of the men of Benjamin, and of Juda to the hold, in which David abode.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	17	And David went out to meet them, and said: If you are come peaceably to me to help me, let my heart be joined to you: but if you plot against me for my enemies whereas I have no iniquity in my hands, let the God of our fathers see, and judge.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	18	But the spirit came upon Amasai the chief among thirty, and he said: We are thine, O David, and for thee, O son of Isai: peace, peace be to thee, and peace to thy helpers. For thy God helpeth thee. So David received them, and made them captains of the band.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	19	And there were some of Manasses that went over to David, when he came with the Philistines against Saul to fight: but he did not fight with them: because the lords of the Philistines taking counsel sent him back, saying: With the danger of our heads he will return to his master Saul.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	20	So when he went back to Siceleg, there fled to him of Manasses, Ednas and Jozabad, and Jedihel, and Michael, and Ednas, and Jozabad, and Eliu, and Salathi, captains of thousands in Manasses.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	21	These helped David against the rovers: for they were all most valiant men, and were made commanders in the army.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	22	Moreover day by day there came some to David to help him till they became a great number, like the army of God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	23	And this is the number of the chiefs of the army who came to David, when he was in Hebron, to transfer to him the kingdom of Saul, according to the word of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	24	The sons of Juda bearing shield and spear, six thousand eight hundred well appointed to war.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	25	Of the sons of Simeon valiant men for war, seven thousand one hundred.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	26	Of the sons of Levi, four thousand six hundred.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	27	And Joiada prince of the race of Aaron, and with him three thousand seven hundred.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	28	Sadoc also a young man of excellent disposition, and the house of his father, twenty-two principal men.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	29	And of the sons of Benjamin the brethren of Saul, three thousand: for hitherto a great part of them followed the house of Saul.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	30	And of the sons of Ephraim twenty thousand eight hundred, men of great valour renowned in their kindreds.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	31	And of the half tribe of Manasses, eighteen thousand, every one by their names, came to make David king.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	32	Also of the sons of Issachar men of understanding, that knew all times to order what Israel should do, two hundred principal men: and all the rest of the tribe followed their counsel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	33	And of Zabulon such as went forth to battle, and stood in array well appointed with armour for war, there came fifty thousand to his aid, with no double heart.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	34	And of Nephtali, a thousand leaders: and with them seven and thirty thousand, furnished with shield and spear.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	35	Of Dan also twenty-eight thousand six hundred prepared for battle.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	36	And of Aser forty thousand going forth to fight, and challenging in battle.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	37	And on the other side of the Jordan of the sons of Ruben, and of Gad, and of the half of the tribe of Manasses a hundred and twenty thousand, furnished with arms for war.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	38	All these men of war well appointed to fight, came with a perfect heart to Hebron, to make David king over all Israel: and all the rest also of Israel, were of one heart to make David king.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	39	And they were there with David three days eating and drinking: for their brethren had prepared for them.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	12	40	Moreover they that were near them even as far as Issachar, and Zabulon, and Nephtali, brought loaves on asses, and on camels, and on mules, and on oxen, to eat: meal, figs, raisins, wine, oil, and oxen, and sheep in abundance, for there was joy in Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	1	And David consulted with the captains of thousands, and of hundreds, and with all the commanders.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	2	And he said to all the assembly of Israel: If it please you; and if the words which I speak come from the Lord our God, let us send to the rest of our brethren into all the countries of Israel, and to the priests, and the Levites, that dwell in the suburbs of the cities, to gather themselves to us,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	3	And let us bring again the ark of our God to us: for we sought it not in the days of Saul.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	4	And all the multitude answered that it should be so: for the word pleased all the people.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	5	So David assembled all Israel from Sihor of Egypt, even to the entering into Emath, to bring the ark of God from Cariathiarim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	6	And David went up with all the men of Israel to the hill of Cariathiarim which is in Juda, to bring thence the ark of the Lord God sitting upon the cherubims, where his name is called upon.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	7	And they carried the ark of God upon a new cart, out of the house of Abinadab. And Oza and his brother drove the cart.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	8	And David and all Israel played before God with all their might with hymns, and with harps, and with psalteries, and timbrels, and cymbals, and trumpets,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	9	And when they came to the floor of Chidon, Oza put forth his hand, to hold up the ark: for the ox being wanton had made it lean a little on one side.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	10	And the Lord was angry with Oza, and struck him, because he had touched the ark; and he died there before the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	11	And David was troubled because the Lord had divided Oza: and he called that place the Breach of Oza to this day.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	12	And he feared God at that time, saying: How can I bring in the ark of God to me?
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	13	And therefore he brought it not home to himself, that is, into the city of David, but carried it aside into the house of Obededom the Gethite.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	13	14	And the ark of God remained in the house of Obededom three months: and the Lord blessed his house, and all that he had.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	1	And Hiram king of Tyre sent messengers to David, and cedar trees, and masons, and carpenters, to build him a house.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	2	And David perceived that the Lord had confirmed him king over Israel, and that his kingdom was exalted over his people Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	3	And David took other wives in Jerusalem: and he beget sons, and daughters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	4	Now these are the names of them that were born to him in Jerusalem: Samua, and Sobad, Nathan, and Solomon,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	5	Jebahar, and Elisua, and Eliphalet,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	6	And Noga, and Napheg, and Japhia,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	7	Elisama. and Baaliada, and Eliphalet.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	8	And the Philistines hearing that David was anointed king over all Israel, went all up to seek him: and David heard of it, and went out against them.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	9	And the Philistines came and spread themselves in the vale of Raphaim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	10	And David consulted the Lord, saying: Shall I go up against the Philistines, and wilt thou deliver them into my hand? And the Lord said to him: Go up, and I will deliver them into thy hand.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	11	And when they were come to Baalpharasim, David defeated them there, and he said: God hath divided my enemies by my hand, as waters are divided: and therefore the name of that place was called Baalpharasim.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	12	And they left there their gods, and David commanded that they should be burnt.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	13	Another time also the Philistines made an irruption, and spread themselves abroad in the valley.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	14	And David consulted God again, and God said to him: Go not up after them, turn away from them, and come upon them over against the pear trees.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	15	And when thou shalt hear the sound of one going in the tops of the pear trees, then shalt thou go out to battle. For God is gone out before thee to strike the army of the Philistines.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	16	And David did as God had commanded him, and defeated the army of the Philistines, slaying them from Gabaon to Gazera.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	14	17	And the name of David became famous in all countries, and the Lord made all nations fear him.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	1	He made also houses for himself in the city of David: and built a place for the ark of God, and pitched a tabernacle for it.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	2	Then David said: No one ought to carry the ark of God, but the Levites, whom the Lord hath chosen to carry it, and to minister unto himself for ever.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	3	And he gathered all Israel together into Jerusalem, that the ark of God might be brought into its place, which he had prepared for it.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	4	And the sons of Aaron also, and the Levites.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	5	Of the children of Caath, Uriel was the chief, and his brethren a hundred and twenty.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	6	Of the sons of Merari, Asaia the chief, and his brethren two hundred and twenty.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	7	Of the sons of Gersom, Joel the chief, and his brethren a hundred and thirty.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	8	Of the sons of Elisaphan, Semeias the chief: and his brethren two hundred.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	9	Of the sons of Hebron, Eliel the chief: and his brethren eighty.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	10	Of the sons of Oziel, Aminadab the chief: and his brethren a hundred and twelve.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	11	And David called Sadoc, and Abiathar the priests, and the Levites, Uriel, Asaia, Joel, Semeia, Eliel, and Aminadab:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	12	And he said to them: You that are the heads of the Levitical families, be sanctified with your brethren, and bring the ark of the Lord the God of Israel to the place, which is prepared for it:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	13	Lest as the Lord at first struck us, because you were not present, the same should now also come to pass, by our doing some thing against the law.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	14	So the priests and the Levites were sanctified, to carry the ark of the Lord the God of Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	15	And the sons of Levi took the ark of God as Moses had commanded, according to the word of the Lord, upon their shoulders, with the staves.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	16	And David spoke to the chiefs of the Levites, to appoint some of their brethren to be singers with musical instruments, to wit, on psalteries, and harps, and cymbals, that the joyful noise might resound on high.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	17	And they appointed Levites, Hemam the son of Joel, and of his brethren Asaph the son of Barachias: and of the sons of Merari, their brethren: Ethan the son of Casaia.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	18	And with them their brethren: in the second rank, Zacharias, and Ben, and Jaziel, and Semiramoth, and Jahiel, and Ani, and Eliab, and Banaias, and Maasias, and Mathathias, and Eliphalu, and Macenias, and Obededom, and Jehiel, the porters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	19	Now the singers, Heman, Asaph, and Ethan, sounded with cymbals of brass.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	20	And Zacharias, and Oziel, and Semiramoth, and Jehiel, and Ani, and Eliab, and Maasias, and Banaias, sung mysteries upon psalteries.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	21	And Mathathias, and Eliphalu, and Macenias and Obededom, and Jehiel and Ozaziu, sung a song of victory for the octave upon harps.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	22	And Chonenias chief of the Levites, presided over the prophecy, to give out the tunes: for he was very skillful.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	23	And Barachias, and Elcana, were doorkeepers of the ark.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	24	And Sebenias, and Josaphat, and Nathanael, and Amasai, and Zacharias, and Banaias, and Eliezer the priests, sounded with trumpets, before the ark of God: and Obededom and Jehias were porters of the ark.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	25	So David and all the ancients of Israel, and the captains over thousands, went to bring the ark of the covenant of the Lord out of the house of Obededom with joy.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	26	And when God had helped the Levites who carried the ark of the covenant of the Lord, they offered in sacrifice seven oxen, and seven rams.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	27	And David was clothed with a robe of fine linen, and all the Levites that carried the ark, and the singing men, and Chonenias the ruler of the prophecy among the singers: and David also had on him an ephod of linen.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	28	And all Israel brought the ark of the covenant of the Lord with joyful shouting, and sounding with the sound of the cornet, and with trumpets, and cymbals, and psalteries, and harps.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	15	29	And when the ark of the covenant of the Lord was come to the city of David, Michol the daughter of Saul looking out at a window, saw king David dancing and playing, and she despised him in her heart.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	1	So they brought the ark of God, and set it in the midst of the tent, which David had pitched for it: and they offered holocausts, and peace offerings before God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	2	And when David had made an end of offering holocausts, and peace offerings, he blessed the people in the name of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	3	And he divided to all and every one, both men and women, a loaf of bread, and a piece of roasted beef, and flour fried with oil.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	4	And he appointed Levites to minister before the ark of the Lord, and to remember his works, and to glorify, and praise the Lord God of Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	5	Asaph the chief, and next after him Zacharias: moreover Jahiel, and Semiramoth, and Jehiel, and Mathathias, and Eliab, and Banaias, and Obededom: and Jehiel over the instruments of psaltery, and harps: and Asaph sounded with cymbals:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	6	But Banaias, and Jaziel the priests, to sound the trumpet continually before the ark of the covenant of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	7	In that day David made Asaph the chief to give praise to the Lord with his brethren.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	8	Praise ye the Lord, and call upon his name: make known his doings among the nations.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	9	Sing to him, yea, sing praises to him: and relate all his wondrous works.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	10	Praise ye his holy name: let the heart of them rejoice, that seek the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	11	Seek ye the Lord, and his power: seek ye his face evermore.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	12	Remember his wonderful works, which he hath done: his signs, and the judgments of his mouth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	13	O ye seed of Israel his servants, ye children of Jacob his chosen.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	14	He is the Lord our God: his judgments are in all the earth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	15	Remember for ever his covenant: the word, which he commanded to a thousand generations.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	16	The covenant which he made with Abraham: and his oath to Isaac.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	17	And he appointed the same to Jacob for a precept: and to Israel for an everlasting covenant:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	18	Saying: To thee will I give the land of Chanaan: the lot of your inheritance.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	19	When they were but a small number: very few and sojourners in it.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	20	And they passed from nation to nation: and from a kingdom to another people.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	21	He suffered no man to do them wrong: and reproved kings for their sake.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	22	Touch not my anointed: and do no evil to my prophets.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	23	Sing ye to the Lord, all the earth: shew forth from day to day his salvation.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	24	Declare his glory among the Gentiles: his wonders among all people.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	25	For the Lord is great and exceedingly to be praised: and he is to be feared above all gods.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	26	For all the gods of the nations are idols: but the Lord made the heavens.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	27	Praise and magnificence are before him: strength and joy in his place.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	28	Bring ye to the Lord, O ye families of the nations: bring ye to the Lord glory and empire.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	29	Give to the Lord glory to his name, bring up sacrifice, and come ye in his sight: and adore the Lord in holy becomingness.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	30	Let all the earth be moved at his presence: for he hath founded the world immoveable.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	31	Let the heavens rejoice, and the earth be glad: and let them say among the nations: The Lord hath reigned.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	32	Let the sea roar, and the fulness thereof: let the fields rejoice, and all things that are in them.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	33	Then shall the trees of the wood give praise before the Lord: because he is come to judge the earth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	34	Give ye glory to the Lord, for he is good: for his mercy endureth for ever.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	35	And say ye: Save us, O God our saviour: and gather us together, and deliver us from the nations, that we may give glory to thy holy name, and may rejoice in singing thy praises.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	36	Blessed be the Lord the God of Israel from eternity to eternity: and let all the people say Amen, and a hymn to God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	37	So he left there before the ark of the covenant of the Lord, Asaph and his brethren to minister in the presence of the ark continually day by day, and in their courses.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	38	And Obededom, with his brethren sixty-eight: and Obededom the son of Idithun, and Hosa he appointed to be porters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	39	And Sadoc the priest, and his brethren priests, before the tabernacle of the Lord in the high place, which was in Gabaon.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	40	That they should offer holocausts to the Lord upon the altar of holocausts continually, morning and evening, according to all that is written in the law of the Lord, which he commanded Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	41	And after him Heman, and Idithun, and the rest that were chosen, every one by his name to give praise to the Lord: because his mercy endureth for ever.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	42	And Heman and Idithun sounded the trumpet, and played on the cymbals, and all kinds of musical instruments to sing praises to God: and the sons of Idithun he made porters.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	16	43	And all the people returned to their houses: and David to bless also his own house.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	1	Now when David was dwelling in his house, he said to Nathan the prophet: Behold I dwell in a house of cedar: and the ark of the covenant of the Lord is under skins.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	2	And Nathan said to David: Do all that is in thy heart: for God is with thee.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	3	Now that night the word of God came to Nathan, saying:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	4	Go, and speak to David my servant: Thus saith the Lord: Thou shalt not build me a house to dwell in.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	5	For I have not remained in a house from the time that I brought up Israel, to this day: but I have been always changing places in a tabernacle, and in a tent,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	6	Abiding with all Israel. Did I ever speak to any one, of all the judges of Israel, whom I charged to feed my people, saying: Why have you not built me a house of cedar?
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	7	Now therefore thus shalt thou say to my servant David: Thus saith the Lord of hosts: I took thee from the pastures, from following the flock, that thou shouldst be ruler of my people Israel.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	8	And I have been with thee whithersoever thou hast gone: and have slain all thy enemies before thee, and have made thee a name like that of one of the great ones that are renowned in the earth.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	9	And I have given a place to my people Israel: they shall be planted, and shall dwell therein, and shall be moved no more, neither shall the children of iniquity waste them, as at the beginning,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	10	Since the days that I gave judges to my people Israel, and have humbled all thy enemies. And I declare to thee, that the Lord will build thee a house.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	11	And when thou shalt have ended thy days to go to thy fathers, I will raise up thy seed after thee, which shall be of thy sons: and I will establish his kingdom.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	12	He shall build me a house, and I will establish his throne for ever.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	13	I will be to him a father, and he shall be to me a son: and I will not take my mercy away from him, as I took it from him that was before thee.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	14	But I will settle him in my house, and in my kingdom for ever: and his throne shall be most firm for ever.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	15	According to all these words, and according to all this vision, so did Nathan speak to David.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	16	And king David came and sat before the Lord, and said: Who am I, O Lord God, and what is my house, that thou shouldst give such things to me?
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	17	But even this hath seemed little in thy sight, and therefore thou hast also spoken concerning the house of thy servant for the time to come: and hast made me remarkable above all men, O Lord God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	18	What can David add more, seeing thou hast thus glorified thy servant, and known him?
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	19	O Lord, for thy servant's sake, according to thy own heart, thou hast shewn all this magnificence, and wouldst have all the great things to be known.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	20	O Lord there is none like thee: and there is no other God beside thee, of all whom we have heard of with our ears.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	21	For what other nation is there upon earth like thy people Israel, whom God went to deliver, and make a people for himself, and by his greatness and terrors cast out nations before their face whom he had delivered out of Egypt?
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	22	And thou hast made thy people Israel to be thy own people for ever, and thou, O Lord, art become their God.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	23	Now therefore, O Lord, let the word which thou hast spoken to thy servant, and concerning his house, be established for ever, and do as thou hast said.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	24	And let thy name remain and be magnified for ever: and let it be said: The Lord of hosts is God of Israel, and the house of David his servant remaineth before him.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	25	For thou, O Lord my God, hast revealed to the ear of thy servant, that thou wilt build him a house: and therefore thy servant hath found confidence to pray before thee.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	26	And now O Lord, thou art God: and thou hast promised to thy servant such great benefits.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	17	27	And thou hast begun to bless the house of thy servant, that it may be always before thee: for seeing thou blessest it, O Lord, it shall be blessed for ever.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	1	And it came to pass after this, that David defeated the Philistines, and humbled them, and took away Geth, and her daughters out of the hands of the Philistines,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	2	And he defeated Moab, and the Moabites were made David's servants, and brought him gifts.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	3	At that time David defeated also Adarezer king of Soba of the land of Hemath, when he went to extend his dominions as far as the river Euphrates.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	4	And David took from him a thousand chariots, and seven thousand horsemen, and twenty thousand footmen, and he houghed all the chariot horses, only a hundred chariots, which he reserved for himself.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	5	And the Syrians of Damascus came also to help Adarezer king of Soba: and David slew of them likewise two and twenty thousand men.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	6	And he put a garrison in Damascus, that Syria also should serve him, and bring gifts. And the Lord assisted him in all things to which he went.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	7	And David took the golden quivers which the servants of Adarezer had, and he brought them to Jerusalem.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	8	Likewise out of Thebath and Chun, cities of Adarezer, he brought very much brass, of which Solomon made the brazen sea, and the pillars, and the vessels of brass.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	9	Now when Thou king of Hemath heard that David had defeated all the army of Adarezer king of Soba,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	10	He sent Adoram his son to king David, to desire peace of him, and to congratulate him that he had defeated and overthrown Adarezer: for Thou was an enemy to Adarezer.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	11	And all the vessels of gold, and silver, and brass king David consecrated to the Lord, with the silver and gold which he had taken from all the nations, as well from Edom, and from Moab, and from the sons of Ammon, as from the Philistines, and from Amalec.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	12	And Abisai the son of Sarvia slew of the Edomites in the vale of the saltpits, eighteen thousand:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	13	And he put a garrison in Edom, that Edom should serve David: and the Lord preserved David in all things to which he went.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	14	So David reigned over all Israel, and executed judgment and justice among all his people.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	15	And Joab the son of Sarvia was over the army, and Josaphat the son of Ahilud recorder.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	16	And Sadoc the son of Achitob, and Achimelech the son of Abiathar, were the priests: and Susa, scribe.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	18	17	And Banaias the son of Joiada was over the bands of the Cerethi, and the Phelethi: and the sons of David were chief about the king.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	1	Now it came to pass that Naas the king of the children of Ammon died, and his son reigned is his stead.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	2	And David said: I will shew kindness to Hanon the son of Naas: for his father did a favour to me. And David sent messengers to comfort him upon the death of his father. But when they were come into the land of the children of Ammon, to comfort Hanon,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	3	The princes of the children of Ammon said to Hanon: Thou thinkest perhaps that David to do honour to thy father hath sent comforters to thee: and thou dost not take notice, that his servants are come to thee to consider, and search, and spy out thy land.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	4	Wherefore Hanon shaved the heads and beards of the servants of David, and cut away their garments from the buttocks to the feet, and sent them away.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	5	And when they were gone, they sent word to David, who sent to meet them (for they had suffered a great affront) and ordered them to stay at Jericho till their beards grew and then to return.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	6	And when the children of Ammon saw that they had done an injury to David, Hanon and the rest of the people sent a thousand talents of silver, to hire them chariots and horsemen out of Mesopotamia, and out of Syria Maacha, and out of Soba.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	7	And they hired two and thirty thousand chariots, and the king of Maacha, with his people. And they came and camped over against Medaba. And the children of Ammon gathered themselves together out of their cities, and came to battle.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	8	And when David heard of it, he sent Joab, and all the army of valiant men:
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	9	And the children of Ammon came out and put their army in array before the gate of the city: and the kings, that were come to their aid, stood apart in the field.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	10	Wherefore Joab understanding that the battle was set against him before and behind, chose out the bravest men of all Israel, and marched against the Syrians,
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	11	And the rest of the people he delivered into the hand of Abisai his brother, and they went against the children of Ammon.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	12	And he said: If the Syrians be too strong for me, then thou shalt help me: but if the children of Ammon be too strong for thee, I will help thee.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	13	Be of good courage and let us behave ourselves manfully for our people, and for the cities of our God: and the Lord will do that which is good in his sight.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	14	So Joab and the people that were with him, went against the Syrians to the battle: and he put them to flight.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	15	And the children of Ammon seeing that the Syrians were fled, they likewise fled from Abisai his brother, and went into the city: and Joab also returned to Jerusalem.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	16	But the Syrians seeing that they had fallen before Israel, sent messengers, and brought to them the Syrians that were beyond the river: and Sophach, general of the army of Adarezer, was their leader.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	17	And it was told David, and he gathered together all Israel, and passed the Jordan, and came upon them, and put his army in array against them, and they fought with him.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	18	But the Syrian fled before Israel: and David slew of the Syrians seven thousand chariots, and forty thousand footmen, and Sophach the general of the army.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	19	19	And when the servants of Adarezer saw themselves overcome by Israel, they went over to David, and served him: and Syria would not help the children of Ammon any more.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	20	1	And it came to pass after the course of a year, at the time that kings go out to battle, Joab gathered together an army and the strength of the troops, and wasted the land of the children of Ammon: and went and besieged Rabba. But David stayed at Jerusalem, when Joab smote Rabba, and destroyed it.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	20	2	And David took the crown of Melchom from his head, and found in it a talent weight of gold, and most precious stones, and he made himself a diadem of it: he took also the spoils of the city which were very great.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	20	3	And the people that were therein he brought out: and made harrows, and sleds, and chariots of iron to go over them, so that they were cut and bruised to pieces: in this manner David dealt with all the cities of the children of Ammon: and he returned with all his people to Jerusalem.
