1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	7	The sons then of Semeias were Othni, and Raphael, and Obed, Elizabad, and his brethren most valiant men: and Eliu, and Samachias.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	8	All these of the sons of Obededom: they, and their sons, and their brethren most able men for service, sixty-two of Obededom.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	9	And the sons of Meselemia, and their brethren strong men, were eighteen.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	10	And of Hosa, that is, of the sons of Merari: Semri the chief, (for he had not a firstborn, and therefore his father made him chief.)
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	11	Helcias the second, Tabelias the third, Zacharias the fourth: all these the sons, and the brethren of Hosa, were thirteen.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	12	Among these were the divisions of the porters, so that the chiefs of the wards, as well as their brethren, always ministered in the house of the Lord.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	13	And they cast lots equally, both little and great, by their families for every one of the gates.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	14	And the lot of the east fell to Selemias. But to his son Zacharias, a very wise and learned man, the north gate fell by lot.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	15	And to Obededom and his sons that towards the south: in which part of the house was the council of the ancients.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	16	To Sephim, and Hosa towards the west, by the gate which leadeth to the way of the ascent: ward against ward.
1 Paralipomena	1Par	13	26	17	Now towards the east were six Levites: and towards the north four a day: and towards the south likewise four a day: and where the council was, two and two.
