1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	5	Then rose up the chief of the fathers of Juda and Benjamin, and the priests, and Levites, and every one whose spirit God had raised up, to go up to build the temple of the Lord, which was in Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	6	And all they that were round about, helped their hands with vessels of silver, and gold, with goods, and with beasts, and with furniture, besides what they had offered on their own accord.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	7	And king Cyrus brought forth the vessels of the temple of the Lord, which Nabuchodonosor had taken from Jerusalem, and had put them in the temple of his god.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	8	Now Cyrus king of Persia brought them forth by the hand of Mithridates the son of Gazabar, and numbered them to Sassabasar the prince of Juda.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	9	And this is the number of them: thirty bowls of gold, a thousand bowls of silver, nine and twenty knives, thirty cups of gold,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	10	Silver cups of a second sort, four hundred and ten: other vessels a thousand.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	1	11	All the vessels of gold and silver, five thousand four hundred: all these Sassabasar brought with them that came up from the captivity of Babylon to Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	1	Now these are the children of the province, that went out of the captivity, which Nabuchodonosor king of Babylon had carried away to Babylon, and who returned to Jerusalem and Juda, every man to his city.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	2	Who came with Zorobabel, Josue, Nehemia, Saraia, Rahelaia, Mardochai, Belsan, Mesphar, Beguai, Rehum, Baana. The number of the men of the people of Israel:
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	3	The children of Pharos two thousand one hundred seventy-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	4	The children of Sephatia, three hundred seventy-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	5	The children of Area, seven hundred seventy-five.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	6	The children of Phahath Moab, of the children of Josue: Joab, two thousand eight hundred twelve.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	7	The children of Elam, a thousand two hundred fifty-four.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	8	The children of Zethua, nine hundred forty-five.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	9	The children of Zachai, seven hundred sixty.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	10	The children of Bani, six hundred forty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	11	The children of Bebai, six hundred twenty-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	12	The children of Azgad, a thousand two hundred twenty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	13	The children of Adonicam, six hundred sixty-six.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	14	The children of Beguai, two thousand fifty-six.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	15	The children of Adin, four hundred fifty-four.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	16	The children of Ather, who were of Ezechias, ninety-eight.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	17	The children of Besai, three hundred and twenty-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	18	The children of Jora, a hundred and twelve.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	19	The children of Hasum, two hundred twenty-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	20	The children of Gebbar, ninety-five.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	21	The children of Bethlehem, a hundred twenty-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	22	The men of Netupha, fifty-six.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	23	The men of Anathoth, a hundred twenty-eight.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	24	The children of Azmaveth, forty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	25	The children of Cariathiarim, Cephira, and Beroth, seven hundred forty-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	26	The children of Rama and Gabaa, six hundred twenty-one.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	27	The men of Machmas, a hundred twenty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	28	The men of Bethel and Hai, two hundred twenty-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	29	The children of Nebo, fifty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	30	The children of Megbis, a hundred fifty-six.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	31	The children of the other Elam, a thousand two hundred fifty-four.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	32	The children of Harim, three hundred and twenty.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	33	The children of Lod, Hadid and One, seven hundred twenty-five.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	34	The children of Jericho, three hundred forty-five.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	35	The children of Senaa, three thousand six hundred thirty.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	36	The priests: the children of Jadaia of the house of Josue, nine hundred seventy-three.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	37	The children of Emmer, a thousand fifty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	38	The children of Pheshur, a thousand two hundred forty-seven.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	39	The children of Harim, a thousand and seventeen.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	40	The Levites: the children of Josue and of Cedmihel, the children of Odovia, seventy-four.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	41	The singing men: the children of Asaph, a hundred twenty-eight.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	42	The children of the porters: the children of Sellum, the children of Ater, the children of Telmon, the children of Accub, the children of Hatita, the children of Sobai: in all a hundred thirty-nine.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	43	The Nathinites: the children of Siha, the children of Hasupha, the children of Tabbaoth,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	44	The children of Ceros, the children of Sia, the children of Phadon,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	45	The children of Lebana, the children of Hegaba, the children of Accub,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	46	The children of Hagab, the children of Semlai, the children of Hanan,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	47	The children of Gaddel, the children of Gaher, the children of Raaia,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	48	The children of Basin, the children of Necoda, the children of Gazam,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	49	The children of Asa, the children of Phasea, the children of Besee,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	50	The children of Asena, the children of Munim, the children of Nephusim,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	51	The children of Bacbuc, the children of Hacupha, the children of Harhur,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	52	The children of Besluth, the children of Mahida, the children of Harsa,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	53	The children of Bercos, the children of Sisara, the children of Thema,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	54	The children of Nasia, the children of Hatipha,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	55	The children of the servants of Solomon, the children of Sotai, the children of Sopheret, the children of Pharuda,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	56	The children of Jala, the children of Dercon, the children of Geddel,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	57	The children of Saphatia, the children of Hatil, the children of Phochereth, which were of Asebaim, the children of Ami,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	58	All the Nathinites, and the children of the servants of Solomon, three hundred ninety-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	59	And these are they that came up from Thelmela, Thelharsa, Cherub, and Adon, and Emer. And they could not shew the house of their fathers and their seed, whether they were of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	60	The children of Dalaia, the children of Tobia, the children of Necoda, six hundred fifty-two.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	61	And of the children of the priests: the children of Hobia, the children of Accos, the children of Berzellai, who took a wife of the daughters of Berzellai, the Galaadite, and was called by their name:
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	62	These sought the writing of their genealogy, and found it not, and they were cast out of the priesthood.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	63	And Athersatha said to them, that they should not eat of the holy of holies, till there arose a priest learned and perfect.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	64	All the multitudes as one man, were forty-two thousand three hundred and sixty:
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	65	Besides their menservants, and womenservants, of whom there were seven thousand three hundred and thirty-seven: and among them singing men, and singing women two hundred.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	66	Their horses seven hundred thirty-six, their mules two hundred forty-five,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	67	Their camels four hundred thirty-five, their asses six thousand seven hundred and twenty.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	68	And some of the chief of the fathers, when they came to the temple of the Lord, which is in Jerusalem, offered freely to the house of the Lord to build it in its place.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	69	According to their ability, they gave towards the expenses of the work, sixty-one thousand solids of gold, five thousand pounds of silver, and a hundred garments for the priests.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	2	70	So the priests and the Levites, and some of the people, and the singing men, and the porters, and the Nathinites dwelt in their cities, and all Israel in their cities.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	1	And now the seventh month was come, and the children of Israel were in their cities: and the people gathered themselves together as one man to Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	2	And Josue the son of Josedec rose up, and his brethren the priests, and Zorobabel the son of Salathiel, and his brethren, and they built the altar of the God of Israel that they might offer holocausts upon it, as it is written in the law of Moses the man of God.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	3	And they set the altar of God upon its bases, while the people of the lands round about put them in fear, and they offered upon it a holocaust to the Lord morning and evening.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	4	And they kept the feast of tabernacles, as it is written, and offered the holocaust every day orderly according to the commandment, the duty of the day in its day.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	5	And afterwards the continual holocaust, both on the new moons, and on all the solemnities of the Lord, that were consecrated, and on all in which a free-will offering was made to the Lord.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	6	From the first day of the seventh month they began to offer holocausts to the Lord: but the temple of God was not yet founded.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	7	And they gave money to hewers of stones and to masons: and meat and drink, and oil to the Sidonians and Tyrians, to bring cedar trees from Libanus to the sea of Joppe, according to the orders which Cyrus king of the Persians had given them.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	8	And in the second year of their coming to the temple of God in Jerusalem, the second month, Zorobabel the son of Salathiel, and Josue the son of Josedec, and the rest of their brethren the priests, and the Levites, and all that were come from the captivity to Jerusalem began, and they appointed Levites from twenty years old and upward, to hasten forward the work of the Lord.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	9	Then Josue and his sons and his brethren, Cedmihel, and his sons, and the children of Juda, as one man, stood to hasten them that did the work in the temple of God: the sons of Henadad, and their sons, and their brethren the Levites.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	10	And when the masons laid the foundations of the temple of the Lord, the priests stood in their ornaments with trumpets: and the Levites the sons of Asaph with cymbals, to praise God by the hands of David king of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	11	And they sung together hymns, and praise to the Lord: because he is good, for his mercy endureth for ever towards Israel. And all the people shouted with a great shout, praising the Lord, because the foundations of the temple of the Lord were laid.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	12	But many of the priests and the Levites, and the chief of the fathers and the ancients that had seen the former temple; when they had the foundation of this temple before their eyes, wept with a loud voice: and many shouting for joy, lifted up their voice.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	3	13	So that one could not distinguish the voice of the shout of joy, from the noise of the weeping of the people: for one with another the people shouted with a loud shout, and the voice was heard afar off.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	1	Now the enemies of Juda and Benjamin heard that the children of the captivity were building a temple to the Lord the God of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	2	And they came to Zorobabel, and the chief of the fathers, and said to them: Let us build with you, for we seek your God as ye do: behold we have sacrificed to him, since the days of Asor Haddan king of Assyria, who brought us hither.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	3	But Zorobabel, and Josue, and the rest of the chief of the fathers of Israel said to them: You have nothing to do with us to build a house to our God, but we ourselves alone will build to the Lord our God, as Cyrus king of the Persians hath commanded us.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	4	Then the people of the land hindered the hands of the people of Juda, and troubled them in building.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	5	And they hired counsellors against them, to frustrate their design all the days of Cyrus king of Persia, even until the reign of Darius king of the Persians.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	6	And in the reign of Assuerus, in the beginning of his reign, they wrote an accusation against the inhabitants of Juda and Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	7	And in the days of Artaxerxes, Beselam, Mithridates, and Thabeel, and the rest that were in the council wrote to Artaxerxes king of the Persians: and the letter of accusation was written in Syriac, and was read in the Syrian tongue.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	8	Reum Beelteem, and Samsai the scribe wrote a letter from Jerusalem to king Artaxerxes, in this manner:
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	9	Reum Beelteem, and Samsai the scribe and the rest of their counsellors, the Dinites, and the Apharsathacites, the Therphalites, the Apharsites, the Erchuites, the Babylonians, the Susanechites, the Dievites, and the Elamites,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	10	And the rest of the nations, whom the great and glorious Asenaphar brought over: and made to dwell in the cities of Samaria and in the rest of the countries of this side of the river in peace.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	11	(This is the copy of the letter, which they sent to him:) To Artaxerxes the king, thy servants, the men that are on this side of the river, send greeting.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	12	Be it known to the king, that the Jews, who came up from thee to us, are come to Jerusalem a rebellious and wicked city, which they are building, setting up the ramparts thereof and repairing the walls.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	13	And now be it known to the king, that if this city be built up, and the walls thereof repaired, they will not pay tribute nor toll, nor yearly revenues, and this loss will fall upon the kings.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	14	But we remembering the salt that we have eaten in the palace, and because we count it a crime to see the king wronged, have therefore sent and certified the king,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	15	That search may be made in the books of the histories of thy fathers, and thou shalt find written in the records: and shalt know that this city is a rebellious city, and hurtful to the kings and provinces, and that wars were raised therein of old time: for which cause also the city was destroyed.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	16	We certify the king, that if this city be built, and the walls thereof repaired, thou shalt have no possession on this side of the river.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	17	The king sent word to Reum Beelteem and Samsai the scribe, and to the rest that were in their council, inhabitants of Samaria, and to the rest beyond the river, sending greeting and peace.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	18	The accusation, which you have sent to us, hath been plainly read before me,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	19	And I commanded: and search hath been made, and it is found, that this city of old time hath rebelled against kings, and seditions and wars have been raised therein.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	20	For there have been powerful kings in Jerusalem, who have had dominion over all the country that is beyond the river: and have received tribute, and toll and revenues.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	21	Now therefore hear the sentence: Hinder those men, that this city be not built, till further orders be given by me.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	22	See that you be not negligent in executing this, lest by little and little the evil grow to the hurt of the kings.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	23	Now the copy of the edict of king Artaxerxes was read before Reum Beelteem, and Samsai the scribe, and their counsellors: and they went up in haste to Jerusalem to the Jews, and hindered them with arm and power.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	4	24	Then the work of the house of the Lord in Jerusalem was interrupted, and ceased till the second year of the reign of Darius king of the Persians.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	1	Now Aggeus the prophet, and Zacharias the son of Addo, prophesied to the Jews that were in Judea and Jerusalem, in the name of the God of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	2	Then rose up Zorobabel the son of Salathiel, and Josue the son of Josedec, and began to build the temple of God in Jerusalem, and with them were the prophets of God helping them.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	3	And at the same time came to them Thathanai, who was governor beyond the river, and Stharbuzanai, and their counsellors: and said thus to them: Who hath given you counsel to build this house, and to repair the walls thereof?
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	4	In answer to which we gave them the names of the men who were the promoters of that building.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	5	But the eye of their God was upon the ancients of the Jews, and they could not hinder them. And it was agreed that the matter should be referred to Darius, and then they should give satisfaction concerning that accusation.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	6	The copy of the letter that Thathanai governor of the country beyond the river, and Stharbuzanai, and his counsellors the Arphasachites, who dwelt beyond the river, sent to Darius the king.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	7	The letter which they sent him, was written thus: To Darius the king all peace.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	8	Be it known to the king, that we went to the province of Judea, to the house of the great God, which they are building with unpolished stones, and timber is laid in the walls: and this work is carried on diligently, and advanceth in their hands.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	9	And we asked those ancients, and said to them thus: Who hath given you authority to build this house, and to repair these walls?
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	10	We asked also of them their names, that we might give thee notice: and we have written the names of the men that are the chief among them.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	11	And they answered us in these words, saying: We are the servants of the God of heaven and earth, and we are building a temple that was built these many years ago, and which a great king of Israel built and set up.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	12	But after that our fathers had provoked the God of heaven to wrath, he delivered them into the hands of Nabuchodonosor the king of Babylon the Chaldean: and he destroyed this house, and carried away the people to Babylon.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	13	But in the first year of Cyrus the king of Babylon, king Cyrus set forth a decree, that this house of God should be built.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	14	And the vessels also of gold and silver of the temple of God, which Nabuchodonosor had taken out of the temple, that was in Jerusalem, and had brought them to the temple of Babylon, king Cyrus brought out of the temple of Babylon, and they were delivered to one Sassabasar, whom also he appointed governor,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	15	And said to him: Take these vessels, and go, and put them in the temple that is in Jerusalem, and let the house of God be built in its place.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	16	Then came this same Sassabasar, and laid the foundations of the temple of God in Jerusalem, and from that time until now it is in building, and is not yet finished.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	5	17	Now therefore if it seem good to the king, let him search in the king's library, which is in Babylon, whether it hath been decreed by Cyrus the king, that the house of God in Jerusalem should be built, and let the king send his pleasure to us concerning this matter.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	1	Then king Darius gave orders, and they searched in the library of the books that were laid up in Babylon,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	2	And there was found in Ecbatana, which is a castle in the province of Media, a book in which this record was written.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	3	In the first year of Cyrus the king: Cyrus the king decreed, that the house of God should be built, which is in Jerusalem, in the place where they may offer sacrifices, and that they lay the foundations that may support the height of threescore cubits, and the breadth of threescore cubits,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	4	Three rows of unpolished stones, and so rows of new timber: and the charges shall be given out of the king's house.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	5	And also let the golden and silver vessels of the temple of God, which Nabuchodonosor took out of the temple of Jerusalem, and brought to Babylon, be restored, and carried back to the temple of Jerusalem to their place, which also were placed in the temple of God.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	6	Now therefore Thathanai, governor of the country beyond the river, Stharbuzanai, and your counsellors the Apharsachites, who are beyond the river, depart far from them,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	7	And let that temple of God be built by the governor of the Jews, and by their ancients, that they may build that house of God in its place.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	8	I also have commanded what must be done by those ancients of the Jews, that the house of God may be built, to wit, that of the king's chest, that is, of the tribute that is paid out of the country beyond the river, the charges be diligently given to those men, lest the work be hindered.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	9	And if it shall be necessary, let calves also, and lambs, and kids, for holocausts to the God of heaven, wheat, salt, wine, and oil, according to the custom of the priests that are in Jerusalem, be given them day by day, that there be no complaint in any thing.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	10	And let them offer oblations to the God of heaven, and pray for the life of the king, and of his children.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	11	And I have made a decree: That if any whosoever, shall alter this commandment, a beam be taken from his house. and set up, and he be nailed upon it, and his house be confiscated.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	12	And may the God, that hath caused his name to dwell there, destroy all kingdoms, and the people that shall put out their hand to resist, and to destroy the house of God, that is in Jerusalem. I Darius have made the decree, which I will have diligently complied with.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	13	So then Thathanai, governor of the country beyond the river, and Stharbuzanai, and his counsellors diligently executed what Darius the king had commanded.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	14	And the ancients of the Jews built and prospered according to the prophecy of Aggeus the prophet, and of Zacharias the son of Addo: and they built and finished, by the commandment of the God of Israel, and by the commandment of Cyrus, and Darius, and Artaxerxes kings of the Persians.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	15	And they were finishing this house of God, until the third day of the month of Adar, which was in the sixth year of the reign of king Darius.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	16	And the children of Israel, the priests and the Levites, and the rest of the children of the captivity kept the dedication of the house of God with joy.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	17	And they offered at the dedication of the house of God, a, hundred calves, two hundred rams, four hundred lambs, and for a sin offering for all Israel twelve he goats, according to the number of the tribes of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	18	And they set the priests in their divisions, and the Levites in their courses over the works of God in Jerusalem, as it is written in the book of Moses.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	19	And the children of Israel of the captivity kept the phase, on the fourteenth day of the first month.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	20	For all the priests and the Levites were purified as one man: all were clear to kill the phase for all the children of the captivity, and for their brethren the priests, and themselves.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	21	And the children of Israel that were returned from captivity, and all that had separated themselves from the filthiness of the nations of the earth to them, to seek the Lord the God of Israel, did eat.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	6	22	And they kept the feast of unleavened bread seven days with joy, for the Lord had made them joyful, and had turned the heart of the king of Assyria to them, that he should help their hands in the work of the house of the Lord the God of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	1	Now after these things in the reign of Artaxerxes king of the Persians, Esdras the son of Saraias, the son of Azarias, the son of Helcias,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	2	The son of Sellum, the son of Sadoc, the son of Achitob,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	3	The son of Amarias, the son of Azarias, the son of Maraioth,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	4	The son of Zarahias, the son of Ozi, the son of Bocci,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	5	The son of Abisue, the son of Phinees, the son of Eleazar the son of Aaron the priest from the beginning.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	6	This Esdras went up from Babylon, and he was a ready scribe in the law of Moses, which the Lord God had given to Israel: and the king granted him all his request, according to the hand of the Lord his God upon him.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	7	And there went up some of the children of Israel, and of the children of the priests, and of the children of the Levites, and of the singing men, and of the porters, and of the Nathinites to Jerusalem in the seventh year of Artaxerxes the king.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	8	And they came to Jerusalem in the fifth month, in the seventh year of the king.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	9	For upon the first day of the first month he began to go up from Babylon, and on the first day of the fifth month he came to Jerusalem according to the good hand of his God upon him.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	10	For Esdras had prepared his heart to seek the law of the Lord, and to do and to teach in Israel the commandments and judgment.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	11	And this is the copy of the letter of the edict, which king Artaxerxes gave to Esdras the priest, the scribe instructed in the words and commandments of the Lord, and his ceremonies in Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	12	Artaxerxes king of kings to Esdras the priest, the most learned scribe of the law of the God of heaven, greeting.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	13	It is decreed by me, that all they of the people of Israel, and of the priests and of the Levites in my realm, that are minded to go into Jerusalem, should go with thee.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	14	For thou art sent from before the king, and his seven counsellors, to visit Judea and Jerusalem according to the law of thy God, which is in thy hand.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	15	And to carry the silver and gold, which the king and his counsellors have freely offered to the God of Israel, whose tabernacle is in Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	16	And all the silver and gold that thou shalt find in all the province of Babylon, and that the people is willing to offer, and that the priests shall offer of their own accord to the house of their God, which is in Jerusalem,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	17	Take freely, and buy diligently with this money, calves, rams, lambs, with the sacrifices and libations of them, and offer them upon the altar of the temple of your God, that is in Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	18	And if it seem good to thee, and to thy brethren to do any thing with the rest of the silver and gold, do it according to the will of your God.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	19	The vessels also, that are given thee for the sacrifice of the house of thy God, deliver thou in the sight of God in Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	20	And whatsoever more there shall be need of for the house of thy God, how much soever thou shalt have occasion to spend, it shall be given out of the treasury, and the king's exchequer, and by me.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	21	I Artaxerxes the king have ordered and decreed to all the keepers of the public chest, that are beyond the river, that whatsoever Esdras the priest, the scribe of the law of the God of heaven, shall require of you, you give it without delay,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	22	Unto a hundred talents of silver, and unto a hundred cores of wheat, and unto a hundred bates of wine, and unto a hundred bates of oil, and salt without measure.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	23	All that belongeth to the rites of the God of heaven, let it be given diligently in the house of the God of heaven: lest his wrath should be enkindled against the realm of the king, and of his sons.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	24	We give you also to understand concerning all the priests, and the Levites, and the singers, and the porters, and the Nathinites, and ministers of the house of this God, that you have no authority to impose toll or tribute, or custom upon them.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	25	And thou Esdras according to the wisdom of thy God, which is in thy hand, appoint judges and magistrates, that may judge all the people, that is beyond the river, that is, for them who know the law of thy God, yea and the ignorant teach ye freely.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	26	And whosoever will not do the law of thy God, and the law of the king diligently, judgment shall be executed upon him, either unto death, or unto banishment, or to the confiscation of goods, or at least to prison.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	27	Blessed be the Lord the God of our fathers, who hath put this in the king's heart, to glorify the house of the Lord, which is in Jerusalem,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	7	28	And hath inclined his mercy toward me before the king and his counsellors, and all the mighty princes of the king: and I being strengthened by the hand of the Lord my God, which was upon me, gathered together out of Israel chief men to go up with me.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	1	Now these are the chiefs of families, and the genealogy of them, who came up with me from Babylon in the reign of Artaxerxes the king.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	2	Of the sons of Phinees, Gersom. Of the sons of Ithamar, Daniel. Of the sons of David, Hattus.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	3	Of the sons of Sechenias, the son of Pharos, Zacharias, and with him were numbered a hundred and fifty men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	4	Of the sons of Phahath Moab, Eleoenai the son of Zareha, and with him two hundred men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	5	Of the sons of Sechenias, the son of Ezechiel, and with him three hundred men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	6	Of the sons of Adan, Abed the son of Jonathan, and with him fifty men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	7	Of the sons of Alam, Isaias the son of Athalias, and with him seventy men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	8	Of the sons of Saphatia: Zebodia the son of Michael, and with him eighty men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	9	Of the sons of Joab, Obedia the son of Jahiel, and with him two hundred and eighteen men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	10	Of the sons of Selomith, the son of Josphia, and with him a hundred and sixty men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	11	Of the sons of Bebai, Zacharias the son of Bebai: and with him eight and twenty men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	12	Of the sons of Azgad, Joanan the son of Eccetan, and with him a hundred and ten men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	13	Of the sons of Adonicam, who were the last: and these are their names: Eliphelet, and Jehiel, and Samaias, and with them sixty men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	14	Of the sons of Begui, Uthai and Zachur, and with them seventy men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	15	And I gathered them together to the river, which runneth down to Ahava, and we stayed there three days: and I sought among the people and among the priests for the sons of Levi, and found none there.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	16	So I sent Eliezer, and Ariel, and Semeias, and Elnathan, and Jarib, and another Elnathan, and Nathan, and Zacharias, and Mosollam, chief men: and Joiarib, and Elnathan, wise men.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	17	And I sent them to Eddo, who is chief in the place of Chasphia, and I put in their mouth the words that they should speak to Eddo, and his brethren the Nathinites in the place of Chasphia, that they should bring us ministers of the house of our God.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	18	And by the good hand of our God upon us, they brought us a most learned man of the sons of Moholi the son of Levi the son of Israel, and Sarabias and his sons, and his brethren eighteen,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	19	And Hasabias, and with him Isaias of the sons of Merari, and his brethren, and his sons twenty.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	20	And of the Nathinites, whom David, and the princes gave for the service of the Levites, Nathinites two hundred and twenty: all these were called by their names.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	21	And I proclaimed there a fast by the river Ahava, that we might afflict ourselves before the Lord our God, and might ask of him a right way for us and for our children, and for all our substance.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	22	For I was ashamed to ask the king for aid and for horsemen, to defend us from the enemy in the way: because we had said to the king: The hand of our God is upon all them that seek him in goodness: and his power and strength, and wrath upon all them that forsake him.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	23	And we fasted, and besought our God for this: and it fell out prosperously unto us.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	24	And I separated twelve of the chief of the priests, Sarabias, and Hasabias, and with them ten of their brethren,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	25	And I weighed unto them the silver and gold, and the vessels consecrated for the house of our God, which the king and his counsellors, and his princes, and all Israel, that were found had offered.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	26	And I weighed to their hands six hundred and fifty talents of silver, and a hundred vessels of silver, and a hundred talents of gold,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	27	And twenty cups of gold, of a thousand solids, and two vessels of the best shining brass, beautiful as gold.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	28	And I said to them: You are the holy ones of the Lord, and the vessels are holy, and the silver and gold, that is freely offered to the Lord the God of our fathers.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	29	Watch ye and keep them, till you deliver them by weight before the chief of the priests, and of the Levites, and the heads of the families of Israel in Jerusalem, into the treasure of the house of the Lord.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	30	And the priests and the Levites received the weight of the silver and gold, and the vessels, to carry them to Jerusalem to the house of our God.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	31	Then we set forward from the river Ahava on the twelfth day of the first month to go to Jerusalem: and the hand of our God was upon us, and delivered us from the hand of the enemy, and of such as lay in wait by the way.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	32	And we came to Jerusalem, and we stayed there three days.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	33	And on the fourth day the silver and the gold, and the vessels were weighed in the house of our God by the hand of Meremoth the son of Urias the priest, and with him was Eleazar the son of Phinees, and with them Jozabad the son of Josue, and Noadaia the son of Benoi, Levites.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	34	According to the number and weight of every thing: and all the weight was written at that time.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	35	Moreover the children of them that had been carried away that were come out of the captivity, offered holocausts to the God of Israel, twelve calves for all the people of Israel, ninety-six rams, seventy-seven lambs, and twelve he goats for sin: all for a holocaust to the Lord.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	8	36	And they gave the king's edicts to the lords that were from the king's court, and the governors beyond the river, and they furthered the people and the house of God.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	1	And after these things were accomplished, the princes came to me, saying: The people of Israel, and the priests and Levites have not separated themselves from the people of the lands, and from their abominations, namely, of the Chanaanites, and the Hethites, and the Pherezites, and the Jebusites, and the Ammonites, and the Moabites, and the Egyptians, and the Amorrhites.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	2	For they have taken of their daughters for themselves and for their sons, and they have mingled the holy seed with the people of the lands. And the hand of the princes and magistrates hath been first in this transgression.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	3	And when I had heard this word, I rent my mantle and my coat, and plucked off the hairs of my head and my beard, and I sat down mourning.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	4	And there were assembled to me all that feared the God of Israel, because of the transgression of those that were come from the captivity, and I sat sorrowful, until the evening sacrifice.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	5	And at the evening sacrifice I rose up from my affliction, and having rent my mantle and my garment, I fell upon my knees, and spread out my hands to the Lord my God,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	6	And said: My God I am confounded and ashamed to lift up my face to thee: for our iniquities are multiplied over our heads, and our sins are grown up even unto heaven,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	7	From the days of our fathers: and we ourselves also have sinned grievously unto this day, and for our iniquities we and our kings, and our priests have been delivered into the hands of the kings of the lands, and to the sword, and to captivity, and to spoil, and to confusion of face, as it is at this day.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	8	And now as a little, and for a moment has our prayer been made before the Lord our God, to leave us a remnant, and give us a pin in his holy place, and that our God would enlighten our eyes, and would give us a little life in our bondage.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	9	For we are bondmen, and in our bondage our God hath not forsaken us, but hath extended mercy upon us before the king of the Persians, to give us life, and to set up the house of our God, and rebuild the desolations thereof, and to give us a fence in Juda and Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	10	And now, O our God, what shall we say after this? for we have forsaken thy commandments,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	11	Which thou hast commanded by the hand of thy servants the prophets, saying: The land which you go to possess, is an unclean land, according to the uncleanness of the people, and of other lands, with their abominations, who have filled it from mouth to mouth with their filth.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	12	Now therefore give not your daughters to their sons, and take not their daughters for your sons, and seek not their peace, nor their prosperity forever: that you may be strengthened, and may eat the good things of the land, and may have your children your heirs for ever.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	13	And after all that is come upon us, for our most wicked deeds, and our great sin, seeing that thou our God hast saved us from our iniquity, and hast given us a deliverance as at this day,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	14	That we should not turn away, nor break thy commandments, nor join in marriage with the people of these abominations. Art thou angry with us unto utter destruction, not to leave us a remnant to be saved?
1 Esdras	Esd	15	9	15	O Lord God of Israel, thou art just: for we remain yet to be saved as at this day. Behold we are before thee in our sin, for there can be no standing before thee in this matter.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	1	Now when Esdras was thus praying, and beseeching, and weeping, and lying before the temple of God, there was gathered to him of Israel an exceeding great assembly of men and women and children, and the people wept with much lamentation.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	2	And Sechenias the son of Jehiel of the sons of Elam answered, and said to Esdras: We have sinned against our God, and have taken strange wives of the people of the land: and now if there be repentance in Israel concerning this,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	3	Let us make a covenant with the Lord our God, to put away all the wives, and such as are born of them, according to the will of the Lord, and of them that fear the commandment of the Lord our God: let it be done according to the law.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	4	Arise, it is thy part to give orders, and we will be with thee: take courage, and do it.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	5	So Esdras arose, and made the chiefs of the priests and of the Levites, and all Israel, to swear that they would do according to this word, and they swore.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	6	And Esdras rose up from before the house of God, and went to the chamber of Johanan the son of Eliasib, and entered in thither: he ate no bread, and drank no water: for he mourned for the transgression of them that were come out of the captivity.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	7	And proclamation was made in Juda and Jerusalem to all the children of the captivity, that they should assemble together into Jerusalem.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	8	And that whosoever would not come within three days, according to the counsel of the princes and the ancients, all his substance should be taken away, and he should be cast out of the company of them that were returned from captivity.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	9	Then all the men of Juda, and Benjamin gathered themselves together to Jerusalem within three days, in the ninth month, the twentieth day of the month: and all the people sat in the street of the house of God, trembling because of the sin, and the rain.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	10	And Esdras the priest stood up, and said to them: You have transgressed, and taken strange wives, to add to the sins of Israel.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	11	And now make confession to the Lord the God of your fathers, and do his pleasure, and separate yourselves from the people of the land, and from your strange wives.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	12	And all the multitude answered and said with a loud voice: According to thy word unto us, so be it done.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	13	But as the people are many, and it is time of rain, and we are not able to stand without, and it is not a work of one day or two, (for we have exceedingly sinned in this matter,)
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	14	Let rulers be appointed in all the multitude: and in all our cities, let them that have taken strange wives come at the times appointed, and with them the ancients and the judges of every city, until the wrath of our God be turned away from us for this sin.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	15	Then Jonathan the son of Azahel, and Jaasia the son of Thecua were appointed over this, and Mesollam and Sebethai, Levites, helped them:
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	16	And the children of the captivity did so. And Esdras the priest, and the men heads of the families in the houses of their fathers, and all by their names, went and sat down in the first day of the tenth month to examine the matter.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	17	And they made an end with all the men that had taken strange wives by the first day of the first month.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	18	And there were found among the sons of the priests that had taken strange wives: Of the sons of Josue the son of Josedec, and his brethren, Maasia, and Eliezer, and Jarib, and Godolia.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	19	And they gave their hands to put away their wives, and to offer for their offence a ram of the flock.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	20	And of the sons of Emmer, Hanani, and Zebedia.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	21	And of the sons of Harim, Maasia, and Elia, and Semeia, and Jehiel, and Ozias.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	22	And of the sons of Pheshur, Elioenai, Maasia, Ismael, Nathanael, Jozabed, and Elasa.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	23	And of the sons of the Levites, Jozabed, and Semei, and Celaia, the same is Calita, Phataia, Juda, and Eliezer.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	24	And of the singing men, Elisiab: and of the porters, Sellum, and Telem, and Uri.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	25	And of Israel, of the sons of Pharos, Remeia, and Jezia, and Melchia, and Miamin, and Eliezer, and Melchia, and Banea.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	26	And of the sons of Elam, Mathania, Zacharias, and Jehiel, and Abdi, and Jerimoth, and Elia.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	27	And of the sons of Zethua, Elioenai, Eliasib, Mathania, Jerimuth, and Zabad, and Aziaza.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	28	And of the sons of Babai, Johanan, Hanania, Zabbai, Athalai:
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	29	And of the sons of Bani, Mosollam, and Melluch, and Adaia, Jasub, and Seal, and Ramoth.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	30	And of the sons of Phahath, Moab, Edna, and Chalal, Banaias, and Maasias, Mathanias, Beseleel, Bennui, and Manasse.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	31	And of the sons of Herem, Eliezer, Josue, Melchias, Semeias, Simeon,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	32	Benjamin, Maloch, Samarias.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	33	And of the sons of Hasom, Mathanai, Mathatha, Zabad, Eliphelet, Jermai, Manasse, Semei.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	34	Of the sons of Bani, Maaddi, Amran, and Uel,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	35	Baneas, and Badaias, Cheliau,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	36	Vania, Marimuth, and Eliasib,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	37	Mathanias, Mathania, and Jasi,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	38	And Bani, and Bennui, Semei,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	39	And Salmias, and Nathan, and Adaias,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	40	And Mechnedebai, Sisai, Sarai,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	41	Ezrel, and Selemiau, Semeria,
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	42	Sellum, Amaria, Joseph.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	43	Of the sons of Nebo, Jehiel, Mathathias, Zabad, Zabina, Jeddu, and Joel, and Banaia.
1 Esdras	Esd	15	10	44	All these had taken strange wives, and there were among them women that had borne children.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	1	The words of Nehemias the son of Helchias. And it came to pass in the month of Casleu, in the twentieth year, as I was in the castle of Susa,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	2	That Hanani one of my brethren came, he and some men of Juda; and I asked them concerning the Jews, that remained and were left of the captivity, and concerning Jerusalem.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	3	And they said to me: They that have remained, and are left of the captivity there in the province, are in great affliction, and reproach: and the wall of Jerusalem is broken down, and the gates thereof are burnt with fire.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	4	And when I had heard these words, I sat down, and wept, and mourned for many days: and I fasted, and prayed before the face of the God of heaven.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	5	And I said: I beseech thee, O Lord God of heaven, strong, great, and terrible, who keepest covenant and mercy with those that love thee, and keep thy commandments:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	6	Let thy ears be attentive, and thy eyes open, to hear the prayer of thy servant, which I pray before thee now, night and day, for the children of Israel thy servants: and I confess the sins of the children of Israel, by which they have sinned against thee: I and my father's house have sinned.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	7	We have been seduced by vanity, and have not kept thy commandments, and ceremonies and judgments, which thou hast commanded thy servant Moses.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	8	Remember the word that thou commandedst to Moses thy servant, saying: If you shall transgress, I will scatter you abroad among the nations:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	9	But if you return to me, and keep my commandments, and do them, though you should be led away to the uttermost parts of the world, I will gather you from thence, and bring you back to the place which I have chosen for my name to dwell there.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	10	And these are thy servants, and thy people: whom thou hast redeemed by thy great strength, and by thy mighty hand.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	1	11	I beseech thee, O Lord, let thy ear be attentive to the prayer of thy servant, and to the prayer of thy servants who desire to fear thy name: and direct thy servant this day, and give him mercy before this man. For I was the king's cupbearer.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	1	And it came to pass in the month of Nisan, in the twentieth year of Artaxerxes the king: that wine was before him, and I took up the wine, and gave it to the king: and I was as one languishing away before his face.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	2	And the king said to me: Why is thy countenance sad, seeing thou dost not appear to be sick? this is not without cause, but some evil, I know not what, is in thy heart. And I was seized with an exceeding great fear:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	3	And I said to the king: O king, live for ever: why should not my countenance be sorrowful, seeing the city of the place of the sepulchres of my fathers is desolate, and the gates thereof are burnt with fire?
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	4	Then the king said to me: For what dost thou make request? And I prayed to the God of heaven,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	5	And I said to the king: If it seem good to the king, and if thy servant hath found favour in thy sight, that thou wouldst send me into Judea to the city of the sepulchre of my father, and I will build it.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	6	And the king said to me, and the queen that sat by him: For how long shall thy journey be, and when wilt thou return? And it pleased the king, and he sent me: and I fixed him a time.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	7	And I said to the king: If it seem good to the king, let him give me letters to the governors of the country beyond the river, that they convey me over, till I come into Judea:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	8	And a letter to Asaph the keeper of the king's forest, to give me timber that I may cover the gates of the tower of the house, and the walls of the city, and the house that I shall enter into. And the king gave me according to the good hand of my God with me.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	9	And I came to the governors of the country beyond the river, and gave them the king's letters. And the king had sent with me captains of soldiers, and horsemen.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	10	And Sanaballat the Horonite, and Tobias the servant, the Ammonite, heard it, and it grieved them exceedingly, that a man was come, who sought the prosperity of the children of Israel.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	11	And I came to Jerusalem, and was there three days.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	12	And I arose in the night, I and some few men with me, and I told not any man what God had put in my heart to do in Jerusalem, and there was no beast with me, but the beast that I rode upon.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	13	And I went out by night by the gate of the valley, and before the dragon fountain, and to the dung gate, and I viewed the wall of Jerusalem which was broken down, and the gates thereof which were consumed with fire.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	14	And I passed to the gate of the fountain, and to the king's aqueduct, and there was no place for the beast on which I rode to pass.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	15	And I went up in the night by the torrent, and viewed the wall, and going back I came to the gate of the valley, and returned.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	16	But the magistrates knew not whither I went, or what I did: neither had I as yet told any thing to the Jews, or to the priests, or to the nobles, or to the magistrates, or to the rest that did the work.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	17	Then I said to them: You know the affliction wherein we are, because Jerusalem is desolate, and the gates thereof are consumed with fire: come, and let us build up the walls of Jerusalem, and let us be no longer a reproach.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	18	And I shewed them how the hand of my God was good with me, and the king's words, which he had spoken to me, and I said: Let us rise up, and build. And their hands were strengthened in good.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	19	But Sanaballat the Horonite, and Tobias the servant, the Ammonite, and Gossem the Arabian heard of it, and they scoffed at us, and despised us, and said: What is this thing that you do? are you going to rebel against the king?
2 Esdras	Neh	16	2	20	And I answered them, and said to them: The God of heaven he helpeth us, and we are his servants: let us rise up and build: but you have no part, nor justice, nor remembrance in Jerusalem.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	1	Then Eliasib the high priest arose, and his brethren the priests, and they built the flock gate: they sanctified it, and set up the doors thereof, even unto the tower of a hundred cubits they sanctified it unto the tower of Hananeel.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	2	And next to him the men of Jericho built: and next to them built Zachur the son of Amri.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	3	But the fish gate the sons of Asnaa built: they covered it, and set up the doors thereof, and tire locks, and the bars. And next to them built Marimuth the son of Urias the son of Accus.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	4	And next to him built Mosollam the son of Barachias, the son of Merezebel, and next to them built Sadoc the son of Baana.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	5	And next to them the Thecuites built: but their great men did not put their necks to the work of their Lord.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	6	And Joiada the son of Phasea, and Mosollam the son of Besodia built the old gate: they covered it and set up the doors thereof, and the locks, and the bars.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	7	And next to them built Meltias the Gabaonite, and Jadon the Meronathite, the men of Gabaon and Maspha, for the governor that was in the country beyond the river.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	8	And next to him built Eziel the son of Araia the goldsmith: and next to him built Ananias the son of the perfumer: and they left Jerusalem unto the wall of the broad street.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	9	And next to him built Raphaia the son of Hur, lord of the street of Jerusalem.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	10	And next to him Jedaia the son of Haromaph over against his own house: and next to him built Hattus the son of Hasebonia.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	11	Melchias the son of Herem, and Hasub the son of Phahath Moab, built half the street, and the tower of the furnaces.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	12	And next to him built Sellum the son of Alohes, lord of half the street of Jerusalem, he and his daughters.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	13	And the gate of the valley Hanun built, and the inhabitants of Zanoe: they built it, and set up the doors thereof, and the locks, and the bars, and a thousand cubits in the wall unto the gate of the dunghill.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	14	And the gate of the dunghill Melchias the son of Rechab built, lord of the street of Bethacharam: he built it, and set up the doors thereof, and the locks, and the bars.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	15	And the gate of the fountain Sellum the son of Cholhoza built, lord of the street of Maspha: he built it, and covered it, and set up the doors thereof, and the locks, and the bars, and the walls of the pool of Siloe unto the king's guard, and unto the steps that go down from the city of David.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	16	After him built Nehemias the son of Azboc, lord of half the street of Bethsur, as far as over against the sepulchre of David, and to the pool, that was built with great labour, and to the house of the mighty.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	17	After him built the Levites, Rehum the son of Benni. After him built Hasebias, lord of half the street of Ceila in his own street.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	18	After him built their brethren Bavai the son of Enadad, lord of half Ceila.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	19	And next to him Aser the son of Josue, lord of Maspha, built another measure, over against the going up of the strong corner.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	20	After him in the mount Baruch the son of Zachai built another measure, from the corner to the door of the house of Eliasib the high priest.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	21	After him Merimuth the son of Urias the son of Haccus, built another measure, from the door of the house of Eliasib, to the end of the house of Eliasib.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	22	And after him built the priests, the men of the plains of the Jordan.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	23	After him built Benjamin and Hasub, over against their own house: and after him built Azarias the son of Maasias the son of Ananias over against his house.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	24	After him built Bennui the son of Hanadad another measure, from the house of Azarias unto the bending, and unto the corner.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	25	Phalel, the son of Ozi, over against the bending and the tower, which lieth out from the king's high house, that is, in the court of the prison: after him Phadaia the son of Pharos.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	26	And the Nathinites dwelt in Ophel, as far as over against the water gate toward the east, and the tower that stood out.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	27	After him the Thecuites built another measure over against, from the great tower that standeth out unto the wall of the temple.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	28	And upward from the horse gate the priests built, every man over against his house.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	29	After them built Sadoc the son of Emmer over against his house. And after him built Semaia the son of Sechenias, keeper of the east gate.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	30	After him built Hanania the son of Selemia, and Hanun the sixth son of Seleph, another measure: after him built Mosollam the son of Barachias over against his treasury. After him Melcias the goldsmith's son built unto the house of the Nathinites, and of the sellers of small wares, over against the judgment gate, and unto the chamber of the corner.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	3	31	And within the chamber of the corner of the flock gate, the goldsmiths and the merchants built.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	1	And it came to pass, that when Sanaballat heard that we were building the wall he was angry: and being moved exceedingly he scoffed at the Jews.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	2	And said before his brethren, and the multitude of the Samaritans: What are the silly Jews doing? Will the Gentiles let them alone? will they sacrifice and make an end in a day? are they able to raise stones out of the heaps of the rubbish, which are burnt?
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	3	Tobias also the Ammonite who was by him said: Let them build: if a fox go up, he will leap over their stone wall.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	4	Hear thou our God, for we are despised: turn their reproach upon their own head, and give them to be despised in a land of captivity.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	5	Cover not their iniquity, and let not their sin be blotted out from before thy face, because they have mocked thy builders.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	6	So we built the wall, and joined it all together unto the half thereof: and the heart of the people was excited to work.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	7	And it came to pass, when Sanaballat, and Tobias, and the Arabians, and the Ammonites, and the Azotians heard that the walls of Jerusalem were made up, and the breaches began to be closed, that they were exceedingly angry.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	8	And they all assembled themselves together, to come, and to fight against Jerusalem, and to prepare ambushes.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	9	And we prayed to our God, and set watchmen upon the wall day and night against them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	10	And Juda said: The strength of the bearer of burdens is decayed, and the rubbish is very much, and we shall not be able to build the wall.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	11	And our enemies said: Let them not know, nor understand, till we come in the midst of them, and kill them, and cause the work to cease.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	12	And it came to pass, that when the Jews that dwelt by them came and told us ten times, out of all the places from whence they came to us,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	13	I set the people in the place behind the wall round about in order, with their swords, and spears, and bows.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	14	And I looked and rose up: and I said to the chief men and the magistrates, and to the rest of the common people: be not afraid of them. Remember the Lord who is great and terrible, and fight for your brethren, your sons, and your daughters, and your wives, and your houses.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	15	And it came to pass, when our enemies heard that the thing had been told us, that God defeated their counsel. And we returned all of us to the walls, every man to his work.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	16	And it came to pass from that day forward, that half of their young men did the work, and half were ready for to fight, with spears, and shields, and bows, and coats of mail, and the rulers were behind them in all the house of Juda.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	17	Of them that built on the wall and that carried burdens, and that laded: with one of his hands he did the work, and with the other he held a sword.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	18	For every one of the builders was girded with a sword about his reins. And they built, and sounded with a trumpet by me.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	19	And I said to the nobles, and to the magistrates, and to the rest of the common people: The work is great and wide, and we are separated on the wall one far from another:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	20	In what place soever you shall hear the sound of the trumpet, run all thither unto us: our God will fight for us.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	21	And let us do the work: and let one half of us hold our spears from the rising of the morning, till the stars appear.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	22	At that time also I said to the people: Let every one with his servant stay in the midst of Jerusalem, and let us take our turns in the night, and by day, to work.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	4	23	Now I and my brethren, and my servants, and the watchmen that followed me, did not put off our clothes: only every man stripped himself when he was to be washed.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	1	Now there was a great cry of the people, and of their wives against their brethren the Jews.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	2	And there were some that said: Our sons and our daughters are very many: let us take up corn for the price of them, and let us eat and live.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	3	And there were some that said: Let us mortgage our lands, and our vineyards, and our houses, and let us take corn because of the famine.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	4	And others said: Let us borrow money for the king's tribute, and let us give up our fields and vineyards:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	5	And now our flesh is as the flesh of our brethren: and our children as their children. Behold we bring into bondage our sons and our daughters, and some of our daughters are bondwomen already, neither have we wherewith to redeem them, and our fields and our vineyards other men possess.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	6	And I was exceedingly angry when I heard their cry according to these words.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	7	And my heart thought with myself: and I rebuked the nobles and magistrates, and said to them: Do you every one exact usury of your brethren? And I gathered together a great assembly against them,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	8	And I said to them: We, as you know, have redeemed according to our ability our brethren the Jews, that were sold to the Gentiles: and will you then sell your brethren, for us to redeem them? And they held their peace, and found not what to answer.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	9	And I said to them: The thing you do is not good: why walk you not in the fear of our God, that we be not exposed to the reproaches of the Gentiles our enemies?
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	10	Both I and my brethren, and my servants, have lent money and corn to many: let us all agree not to call for it again; let us forgive the debt that is owing to us.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	11	Restore ye to them this day their fields, and their vineyards, and their oliveyards, and their houses: and the hundredth part of the money, and of the corn, the wine, and the oil, which you mere wont to exact of them, give it rather for them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	12	And they said: We will restore, and we will require nothing of them: and we will do as thou sayest. And I called the priests and took an oath of them, to do according to what I had said.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	13	Moreover I shook my lap, and said: So may God shake every man that shall not accomplish this word, out of his house, and out of his labours, thus may he be shaken out, and become empty. And all the multitude said: Amen. And they praised God. And the people did according to what was said.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	14	And from the day, in which the king commanded me to be governor in the land of Juda, from the twentieth year even to the two and thirtieth year of Artaxerxes the king, for twelve years, I and my brethren did not eat the yearly allowance that was due to the governors.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	15	But the former governors that had been before me, were chargeable to the people, and took of them in bread, and wine, and in money every day forty sicles: and their officers also oppressed the people. But I did not so for the fear of God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	16	Moreover I built in the work of the wall, and I bought no land, and all my servants were gathered together to the work.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	17	The Jews also and the magistrates to the number of one hundred and fifty men, were at my table, besides them that came to us from among the nations that were round about us.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	18	And there was prepared for me day by day one ox, and six choice rams, besides fowls, and once in ten days I gave store of divers wines, and many other things: yet I did not require my yearly allowance as governor: for the people were very much impoverished.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	5	19	Remember me, O my God, for good according to all that I have done for this people.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	1	And it came to pass, when Sanaballat, and Tobias, and Gossem the Arabian, and the rest of our enemies, heard that I had built the wall, and that there was no breach left in it, (though at that time I had not set up the doors in the gates,)
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	2	Sanaballat and Gossem sent to me, saying: Come, and let us make a league together in the villages, in the plain of Ono. But they thought to do me mischief.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	3	And I sent messengers to them, saying: I am doing a great work, and I cannot come down, lest it be neglected whilst I come, and go down to you.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	4	And they sent to me according to this word, four times: and I answered them after the same manner.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	5	And Sanaballat sent his servant to me the fifth time according to the former word, and he had a letter in his hand written in this manner:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	6	It is reported amongst the Gentiles, and Gossem hath said it, that thou and the Jews think to rebel, and therefore thou buildest the wall, and hast a mind to set thyself king over them: for which end
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	7	Thou hast also set up prophets, to preach of thee at Jerusalem, saying: There is a king in Judea. The king will hear of these things: therefore come now, that we may take counsel together.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	8	And I sent to them, saying: There is no such thing done as thou sayest: but thou feignest these things out of thy own heart.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	9	For all these men thought to frighten us, thinking that our hands would cease from the work, and that we would leave off. Wherefore I strengthened my hands the more:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	10	And I went into the house of Samaia the son of Delaia, the son of Metabeel privately. And he said: Let us consult together in the house of God in the midst of the temple: and let us shut the doors of the temple, for they will come to kill thee, and in the night they will come to slay thee.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	11	And I said: Should such a man as I flee? and who is there that being as I am, would go into the temple, to save his life? I will not go in.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	12	And I understood that God had not sent him, but that he had spoken to me as if he had been prophesying, and Tobias, and Sanaballat had hired him.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	13	For he had taken money, that I being afraid should do this thing, and sin, and they might have some evil to upbraid me withal.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	14	Remember me, O Lord, for Tobias and Sanaballat, according to their works of this kind: and Noadias the prophet, and the rest of the prophets that would have put me in fear.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	15	But the wall was finished the five and twentieth day of the month of Elul, in two and fifty days.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	16	And it came to pass when all our enemies heard of it, that all nations which were round about us, were afraid, and were cast down within themselves, for they perceived that this work was the work of God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	17	Moreover in those days many letters were sent by the principal men of the Jews to Tobias, and from Tobias there came letters to them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	18	For there were many in Judea sworn to him, because he was the son in law of Sechenias the son of Area, and Johanan his son had taken to wife the daughter of Mosollam the son of Barachias.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	6	19	And they praised him also before me, and they related my words to him: And Tobias sent letters to put me in fear.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	1	Now after the wall was built, and I had set up the doors, and numbered the porters and singing men, and Levites:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	2	I commanded Hanani my brother, and Hananias ruler of the house of Jerusalem, (for he seemed as a sincere man, and one that feared God above the rest,)
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	3	And I said to them: Let not the gates of Jerusalem be opened till the sun be hot. And while they were yet standing by, the gates were shut, and barred: and I set watchmen of the inhabitants of Jerusalem, every one by their courses, and every man over against his house.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	4	And the city was very wide and great, and the people few in the midst thereof, and the houses were not built.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	5	But God had put in my heart, and I assembled the princes and magistrates, and common people, to number them: and I found a book of the number of them who came up at first, and therein it was found written:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	6	These are the children of the province, who came up from the captivity of them that had been carried away, whom Nabuchodonosor the king of Babylon had carried away, and who returned into Judea, every one into his own city.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	7	Who came with Zorobabel, Josue, Nehemias, Azarias, Raamias, Nahamani, Mardochai, Belsam, Mespharath, Begoia, Nahum, Baana. The number of the men of the people of Israel:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	8	The children of Pharos, two thousand one hundred seventy-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	9	The children of Sephatia, three hundred seventy-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	10	The children of Area, six hundred fifty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	11	The children of Phahath Moab of the children of Josue and Joab, two thousand eight hundred eighteen.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	12	The children of Elam, one thousand two hundred fifty-four.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	13	The children of Zethua, eight hundred forty-five.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	14	The children of Zachai, seven hundred sixty.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	15	The children of Bannui, six hundred forty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	16	The children of Bebai, six hundred twenty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	17	The children of Azgad, two thousand three hundred twenty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	18	The children of Adonicam, six hundred sixty-seven.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	19	The children of Beguai, two thousand sixty-seven.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	20	The children of Adin, six hundred fifty-five.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	21	The children of Ater, children of Hezechias, ninety-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	22	The children of Hasem, three hundred twenty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	23	The children of Besai, three hundred twenty-four.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	24	The children of Hareph, a hundred and twelve.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	25	The children of Gabaon, ninety-five.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	26	The children of Bethlehem, and Netupha, a hundred eighty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	27	The men of Anathoth, a hundred twenty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	28	The men of Bethazmoth, forty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	29	The men of Cariathiarim, Cephira, and Beroth, seven hundred forty-three.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	30	The men of Rama and Geba, six hundred twenty-one.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	31	The men of Machmas, a hundred twenty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	32	The men of Bethel and Hai, a hundred twenty-three.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	33	The men of the other Nebo, fifty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	34	The men of the other Elam, one thousand two hundred fifty-four.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	35	The children of Harem, three hundred and twenty.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	36	The children of Jericho, three hundred forty-five.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	37	The children of Led, of Hadid and One, seven hundred twenty-one.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	38	The children of Senaa, three thousand nine hundred thirty.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	39	The priests: the children of Idaia in the house of Josue, nine hundred and seventy-three.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	40	The children of Emmer, one thousand fifty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	41	The children of Phashur, one thousand two hundred forty-seven.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	42	The children of Arem, one thousand and seventeen. The Levites:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	43	The children of Josue and Cedmihel, the sons
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	44	Of Oduia, seventy-four. The singing men:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	45	The children of Asaph, a hundred forty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	46	The porters: the children of Sellum, the children of Ater, the children of Telmon, the children of Accub, the children of Hatita, the children of Sobai: a hundred thirty-eight.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	47	The Nathinites: the children of Soha, the children of Hasupha, the children of Tebbaoth,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	48	The children of Ceros, the children of Siaa, the children of Phadon, the children of Lebana, the children of Hagaba, the children of Selmai,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	49	The children of Hanan, the children of Geddel, the children of Gaher,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	50	The children of Raaia, the children of Rasin, the children of Necoda,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	51	The children of Gezem, the children of Asa, the children of Phasea,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	52	The children of Besai, the children of Munim, the children of Nephussim,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	53	The children of Bacbuc, the children of Hacupha, the children of Harhur,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	54	The children of Besloth, the children of Mahida, the children of Harsa,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	55	The children of Bercos, the children of Sisara, the children of Thema,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	56	The children of Nasia, the children of Hatipha,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	57	The children of the servants of Solomon, the children of Sothai, the children of Sophereth, the children of Pharida,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	58	The children of Jahala, the children of Darcon, the children of Jeddel,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	59	The children of Saphatia, the children of Hatil, the children of Phochereth, who was born of Sabaim, the son of Amon.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	60	All the Nathinites, and the children of the servants of Solomon, three hundred ninety-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	61	And these are they that came up from Telmela, Thelharsa, Cherub, Addon, and Emmer: and could not shew the house of their fathers, nor their seed, whether they were of Israel.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	62	The children of Dalaia, the children of Tobia, the children of Necoda, six hundred forty-two.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	63	And of the priests, the children of Habia, the children of Accos, the children of Berzellai, who took a wife of the daughters of Berzellai the Galaadite, and he was called by their name.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	64	These sought their writing in the record, and found it not: and they were cast out of the priesthood.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	65	And Athersatha said to them, that they should not eat of the holies of holies, until there stood up a priest learned and skillful.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	66	All the multitude as it were one man, forty-two thousand three hundred sixty,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	67	Beside their menservants and womenservants, who were seven thousand three hundred thirty-seven: and among them singing men, and singing women, two hundred forty-five.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	68	Their horses, seven hundred thirty-six: their mules two hundred forty-five:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	69	Their camels, four hundred thirty-five, their asses, six thousand seven hundred and twenty.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	70	And some of the heads of the families gave unto the work. Athersatha gave into the treasure a thousand drama of gold, fifty bowls, and five hundred and thirty garments for priests.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	71	And some of the heads of families gave to the treasure of the work, twenty thousand drama of gold, and two thousand two hundred pounds of silver.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	72	And that which the rest of the people gave, was twenty thousand drama of gold, and two thousand pounds of silver, and sixty-seven garments for priests.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	7	73	And the priests, and the Levites, and the porters, and the singing men, and the rest of the common people, and the Nathinites, and all Israel dwelt in their cities.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	1	And the seventh month came: and the children of Israel were in their cities. And all the people were gathered together as one man to the street which is before the water gate, and they spoke to Esdras the scribe, to bring the book of the law of Moses, which the Lord had commanded to Israel.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	2	Then Esdras the priest brought the law before the multitude of men and women, and all those that could understand, in the first day of the seventh month.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	3	And he read it plainly in the street that was before the water gate, from the morning until midday, before the men, and the women, and all those that could understand: and the ears of all the people were attentive to the book.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	4	And Esdras the scribe stood upon a step of wood, which he had made to speak upon, and there stood by him Mathathias, and Semeia, and Ania, and Uria, and Helcia, and Maasia, on his right hand: and on the left, Phadaia, Misael, and Melchia, and Hasum, and Hasbadana, Zacharia and Mosollam.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	5	And Esdras opened the book before all the people: for he was above all the people: and when he had opened it, all the people stood.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	6	And Esdras blessed the Lord the great God: and all the people answered, Amen, amen: lifting up their hands: and they bowed down, and adored God with their faces to the ground.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	7	Now Josue, and Bani, and Serebia, Jamin, Accub, Sephtai, Odia, Maasia, Celtia, Azarias, Jozabed, Hanan, Phalaia, the Levites, made silence among the people to hear the law: and the people stood in their place.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	8	And they read in the book of the law of God distinctly and plainly to be understood: and they understood when it was read.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	9	And Nehemias (he is Athersatha) and Esdras the priest and scribe, and the Levites who interpreted to all the people, said: This is a holy day to the Lord our God: do not mourn, nor weep: for all the people wept, when they heard the words of the law.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	10	And he said to them: Go, eat fat meats, and drink sweet wine, and send portions to them that have not prepared for themselves: because it is the holy day of the Lord, and be not sad: for the joy of the Lord is our strength.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	11	And the Levites stilled all the people, saying: Hold your peace, for the day is holy, and be not sorrowful.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	12	So all the people went to eat and drink, and to send portions, and to make great mirth: because they understood the words that he had taught them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	13	And on the second day the chiefs of the families of all the people, the priests, and the Levites were gathered together to Esdras the scribe, that he should interpret to them the words of the law.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	14	And they found written in the law, that the Lord had commanded by the hand of Moses, that the children of Israel should dwell in tabernacles, on the feast, in the seventh month:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	15	And that they should proclaim and publish the word in all their cities, and in Jerusalem, saying: Go forth to the mount, and fetch branches of olive, and branches of beautiful wood, branches of myrtle, and branches of palm, and branches of thick trees, to make tabernacles, as it is written.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	16	And the people went forth, and brought. And they made themselves tabernacles every man on the top of his house, and in their courts, and in the courts of the house of God, and in the street of the water gate, and in the street of the gate of Ephraim.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	17	And all the assembly of them that were returned from the captivity, made tabernacles, and dwelt in tabernacles: for since the days of Josue the son of Nun the children of Israel had not done so, until that day: and there was exceeding great joy.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	8	18	And he read in the book of the law of God day by day, from the first day till the last, and they kept the solemnity seven days, and in the eighth day a solemn assembly according to the manner.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	1	And in the four and twentieth day of the month the children of Israel came together with fasting and with sackcloth, and earth upon them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	2	And the seed of the children of Israel separated themselves from every stranger: and they stood, and confessed their sins, and the iniquities of their fathers.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	3	And they rose up to stand: and they read in the book of the law of the Lord their God, four times in the day, and four times they confessed, and adored the Lord their God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	4	And there stood up upon the seep of the Levites, Josue, and Bani, and Cedmihel, Sabania, Bonni, Sarebias, Bani, and Chanani: and they cried with a loud voice to the Lord their God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	5	And the Levites Josue and Cedmihel, Bonni, Hasebnia, Serebia, Oduia, Sebnia, and Phathahia, said: Arise, bless the Lord your God from eternity to eternity: and blessed be the high name of thy glory with all blessing and praise.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	6	Thou thyself, O Lord alone, thou hast made heaven, and the heaven of heavens, and all the host thereof: the earth and all things that are in it: the seas and all that are therein: and thou givest life to all these things, and the host of heaven adoreth thee.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	7	Thou, O Lord God, art he who chosest Abram, and broughtest him forth out of the fire of the Chaldeans, and gavest him the name of Abraham.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	8	And thou didst find his heart faithful before thee: and thou madest a covenant with him, to give him the land of the Chanaanite, of the Hethite, and of the Amorrhite, and of the Pherezite, and of the Jebusite, and of the Gergezite, to give it to his seed: and thou hast fulfilled thy words, because thou art just.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	9	And thou sawest the affliction of our fathers in Egypt: and thou didst hear their cry by the Red Sea.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	10	And thou shewedst signs and wonders upon Pharao, and upon all his servants, and upon the people of his land: for thou knewest that they dealt proudly against them: and thou madest thyself a name, as it is at this day.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	11	And thou didst divide the sea before them, and they passed through the midst of the sea on dry land: but their persecutors thou threwest into the depth, as a stone into mighty waters.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	12	And in a pillar of a cloud thou wast their leader by day, and in a pillar of fire by night, that they might see the way by which they went.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	13	Thou camest down also to mount Sinai, and didst speak with them from heaven, and thou gavest them right judgments, and the law of truth, ceremonies, and good precepts.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	14	Thou madest known to them thy holy sabbath, and didst prescribe to them commandments, and ceremonies, and the law by the hand of Moses thy servant.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	15	And thou gavest them bread from heaven in their hunger, and broughtest forth water for them out of the rock in their thirst, and thou saidst to them that they should go in, and possess the land, upon which thou hadst lifted up thy hand to give it them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	16	But they and our fathers dealt proudly, and hardened their necks and hearkened not to thy commandments.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	17	And they would not hear, and they remembered not thy wonders which thou hadst done for them. And they hardened their necks, and gave the head to return to their bondage, as it were by contention. But thou, a forgiving God, gracious, and merciful, longsuffering, and full of compassion, didst not forsake them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	18	Yea when they had made also to themselves a molten calf, and had said: This is thy God, that brought thee out of Egypt: and had committed great blasphemies:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	19	Yet thou, in thy many mercies, didst not leave them in the desert: the pillar of the cloud departed not from them by day to lead them in the way, and the pillar of fire by night to shew them the way by which they should go.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	20	And thou gavest them thy good Spirit to teach them, and thy manna thou didst not withhold from their mouth, and thou gavest them water for their thirst.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	21	Forty years didst thou feed them in the desert, and nothing was wanting to them: their garments did not grow old, and their feet were not worn.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	22	And thou gavest them kingdoms, and nations, and didst divide lots for them: and they possessed the land of Sehon, and the land of the king of Hesebon, and the land of Og king of Basan.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	23	And thou didst multiply their children as the stars of heaven, and broughtest them to the land concerning which thou hadst said to their fathers, that they should go in and possess it.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	24	And the children came and possessed the land, and thou didst humble before them the inhabitants of the land, the Chanaanites, and gavest them into their hands, with their kings, and the people of the land, that they might do with them as it pleased them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	25	And they took strong cities and a fat land, and possessed houses full of all goods: cisterns made by others, vineyards, and oliveyards, and fruit trees in abundance: and they ate, and were filled, and became fat, and abounded with delight in thy great goodness.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	26	But they provoked thee to wrath, and departed from thee, and threw thy law behind their backs: and they killed thy prophets, who admonished them earnestly to return to thee: and they were guilty of great blasphemies.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	27	And thou gavest them into the hands of their enemies, and they afflicted them. And in the time of their tribulation they cried to thee, and thou heardest from heaven, and according to the multitude of thy tender mercies thou gavest them saviours, to save them from the hands of their enemies.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	28	But after they had rest, they returned to do evil in thy sight: and thou leftest them in the hand of their enemies, and they had dominion over them. Then they returned, and cried to thee: and thou heardest from heaven, and deliveredst them many times in thy mercies.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	29	And thou didst admonish them to return to thy law. But they dealt proudly, and hearkened not to thy commandments, but sinned against thy judgments, which if a man do, he shall live in them: and they withdrew the shoulder, and hardened their neck, and would not hear.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	30	And thou didst forbear with them for many years, and didst testify against them by thy spirit by the hand of thy prophets: and they heard not, and thou didst deliver them into the hand of the people of the lands.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	31	Yet in thy very many mercies thou didst not utterly consume them, nor forsake them: because thou art a merciful and gracious God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	32	Now therefore our God, great, strong and terrible, who keepest covenant and mercy, turn not away from thy face all the labour which hath come upon us, upon our kings, and our princes, and our priests, and our prophets, and our fathers, and all the people from the days of the king of Assur, until this day.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	33	And thou art just in all things that have come upon us: because thou hast done truth, but we have done wickedly.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	34	Our kings, our princes, our priests, and our fathers have not kept thy law, and have not minded thy commandments, and thy testimonies which thou hast testified among them.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	35	And they have not served thee in their kingdoms, and in thy manifold goodness, which thou gavest them, and in the large and fat land, which thou deliveredst before them, nor did they return from their most wicked devices.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	36	Behold we ourselves this day are bondmen: and the land, which thou gavest our fathers, to eat the bread thereof, and the good things thereof, and we ourselves are servants in it.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	37	And the fruits thereof grow up for the kings, whom thou hast set over us for our sins, and they have dominion over our bodies, and over our beasts, according to their will, and we are in great tribulation.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	9	38	And because of all this we ourselves make a covenant, and write it, and our princes, our Levites, and our priests sign it.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	10	1	And the subscribers were Nehemias, Athersatha the son of Hachelai, and Sedecias,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	10	2	Saraias, Azarias, Jeremias,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	10	3	Pheshur, Amarias, Melchias,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	10	4	Hattus, Sebenia, Melluch,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	10	5	Harem, Merimuth, Obdias,
