2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	1	Now these are the priests and the Levites, that went up with Zorobabel the son of Salathiel, and Josue: Saraia, Jeremias, Esdras,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	2	Amaria, Melluch, Hattus,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	3	Sebenias, Rheum, Merimuth,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	4	Addo, Genthon, Abia,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	5	Miamin, Madia, Belga,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	6	Semeia, and Joiarib, Idaia, Sellum, Amoc, Helcias,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	7	Idaia. These were the chief of the priests, and of their brethren in the days of Josue.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	8	And the Levites, Jesua, Bennui, Cedmihel, Sarebia, Juda, Mathanias, they and their brethren were over the hymns:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	9	And Becbecia, and Hanni, and their brethren every one in his office.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	10	And Josue beget Joacim, and Joacim beget Eliasib, and Eliasib beget Joiada,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	11	And Joiada beget Jonathan, and Jonathan beget Jeddoa.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	12	And in the days of Joacim the priests and heads of the families were: Of Saraia, Maraia: of Jeremias, Hanania:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	13	Of Esdras, Mosollam: and of Amaria, Johanan:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	14	Of Milicho, Jonathan: of Sebenia, Joseph:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	15	Of Haram, Edna: of Maraioth, Helci:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	16	Of Adaia, Zacharia: of Genthon, Mosollam:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	17	Of Abia, Zechri: of Miamin and Moadia, Phelti:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	18	Of Belga, Sammua of Semaia, Jonathan:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	19	Of Joiarib, Mathanai: of Jodaia, Azzi:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	20	Of Sellai, Celai: of Amoc, Heber:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	21	Of Helcias, Hasebia: of Idaia, Nathanael.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	22	The Levites the chiefs of the families in the days of Eliasib, and Joiada, and Johanan, and Jeddoa, were recorded, and the priests in the reign of Darius the Persian.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	23	The sons of Levi, heads of the families were written in the book of Chronicles, even unto the days of Jonathan the son of Eliasib.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	24	Now the chief of the Levites were Hasebia, Serebia, and Josue the son of Cedmihel: and their brethren by their courses, to praise and to give thanks according to the commandment of David the man of God, and to wait equally in order.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	25	Mathania, and Becbecia, Obedia, and Mosollam, Telmon, Accub, were keepers of the gates and of the entrances before the gates.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	26	These were in the days of Joacim the son of Josue, the son of Josedec, and in the days of Nehemias the governor, and of Esdras the priest and scribe.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	27	And at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem they sought the Levites out of all their places, to bring them to Jerusalem, and to keep the dedication, and to rejoice with thanksgiving, and with singing, and with cymbals, and psalteries and harps.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	28	And the sons of the singing men were gathered together out of the plain country about Jerusalem, and out of the villages of Nethuphati,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	29	And from the house of Galgal, and from the countries of Geba and Azmaveth: for the singing men had built themselves villages round about Jerusalem.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	30	And the priests and the Levites purified, and they purified the people, and the gates, and the wall.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	31	And I made the princes of Juda go up upon the wall, and I appointed two great choirs to give praise. And they went on the right hand upon the wall toward the dunghill gate.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	32	And after them went Osaias, and half of the princes of Juda,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	33	And Azarias, Esdras, and Mosollam, Judas, and Benjamin, and Semeia, and Jeremias.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	34	And of the sons of the priests with trumpets, Zacharias the son of Jonathan. the son of Semeia, the son of Mathania; the son of Michaia, the son of Zechur, the son of Asaph,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	35	And his brethren Semeia, and Azareel Malalai, Galalai, Maai, Nathanael, and Judas, and Hanani, with the musical instruments of David the man of God: and Esdras the scribe before them at the fountain gate.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	36	And they went up over against them by the stairs of the city of David, at the going up of the wall of the house of David, and to the water gate eastward:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	37	And the second choir of them that gave thanks went on the opposite side, and I after them, and the half of the people upon the wall, and upon the tower of the furnaces, even to the broad wall,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	38	And above the gate of Ephraim, and above the old gate, and above the fish gate and the tower of Hananeel, and the tower of Emath, and even to the flock gate: and they stood still in the watch gate.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	39	And the two choirs of them that gave praise stood still at the house of God, and I and the half of the magistrates with me.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	40	And the priests, Eliachim, Maasia, Miamin, Michea, Elioenai, Zacharia, Hanania with trumpets,
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	41	And Maasia, and Semeia, and Eleazar, and Azzi, and Johanan, and Melchia, and Elam, and Ezer. And the singers sung loud, and Jezraia was their overseer:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	42	And they sacrificed on that day great sacrifices, and they rejoiced: for God had made them joyful with great joy: their wives also and their children rejoiced, and the joy of Jerusalem was heard afar off.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	43	They appointed also in that day men over the storehouses of the treasure, for the libations, and for the firstfruits, and for the tithes, that the rulers of the city might bring them in by them in honour of thanksgiving, for the priests and Levites: for Juda was joyful in the priests and Levites that assisted.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	44	And they kept the watch of their God, and the observance of expiation, and the singing men, and the porters, according to the commandment of David, and of Solomon his son.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	45	For in the days of David and Asaph from the beginning there were chief singers appointed, to praise with canticles, and give thanks to God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	12	46	And all Israel, in the days of Zorobabel, and in the days of Nehemias gave portions to the singing men, and to the porters, day by day, and they sanctified the Levites, and the Levites sanctified the sons of Aaron.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	1	And on that day they read in the book of Moses in the hearing of the people: and therein was found written, that the Ammonites and the Moabites should not come in to the church of God for ever:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	2	Because they met not the children of Israel with bread and water: and they hired against them Balaam, to curse them, and our God turned the curse into blessing.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	3	And it came to pass, when they had heard the law, that they separated every stranger from Israel.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	4	And over this thing was Eliasib the priest, who was set over the treasury of the house of our God, and was near akin to Tobias.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	5	And he made him a great storeroom, where before him they laid up gifts, and frankincense, and vessels, and the tithes of the corn, of the wine, and of the oil, the portions of the Levites, and of the singing men, and of the porters, and the firstfruits of the priests.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	6	But in all this time I was not in Jerusalem, because in the two and thirtieth year of Artaxerxes king of Babylon, I went to the king, and after certain days I asked the king:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	7	And I came to Jerusalem, and I understood the evil that Eliasib had done for Tobias, to make him a storehouse in the courts of the house of God.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	8	And it seemed to me exceeding evil. And I cast forth the vessels of the house of Tobias out of the storehouse.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	9	And I commanded and they cleansed the storehouses: and I brought thither again the vessels of the house of God, the sacrifice, and the frankincense.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	10	And I perceived that the portions of the Levites had not been given them: and that the Levites, and the singing men, and they that ministered were fled away every man to his own country:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	11	And I pleaded the matter against the magistrates, and said: Why have we forsaken the house of God? And I gathered them together, and I made them to stand in their places.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	12	And all Juda brought the tithe of the corn, and the wine, and the oil into the storehouses.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	13	And we set over the storehouses Selemias the priest, and Sadoc the scribe, and of the Levites Phadaia, and next to them Hanan the son of Zachur, the son of Mathania: for they were approved as faithful, and to them were committed the portions of their brethren.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	14	Remember me, O my God, for this thing, and wipe not out my kindnesses, which I have done relating to the house of my God and his ceremonies.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	15	In those days I saw in Juda some treading the presses on the sabbath, and carrying sheaves, and lading asses with wine, and grapes, and figs, and all manner of burthens, and bringing them into Jerusalem on the sabbath day. And I charged them that they should sell on a day on which it was lawful to sell.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	16	Some Tyrians also dwelt there, who brought fish, and all manner of wares: and they sold them on the sabbaths to the children of Juda in Jerusalem.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	17	And I rebuked the chief men of Juda, and said to them: What is this evil thing that you are doing, profaning the sabbath day?
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	18	Did not our fathers do these things, and our God brought all this evil upon us, and upon this city? And you bring more wrath upon Israel by violating the sabbath.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	19	And it came to pass, that when the gates of Jerusalem were at rest on the sabbath day, I spoke: and they shut the gates, and I commanded that they should not open them till after the sabbath: and I set some of my servants at the gates, that none should bring in burthens on the sabbath day.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	20	So the merchants, and they that sold all kinds of wares, stayed without Jerusalem once or twice.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	21	And I charged them, and I said to them: Why stay you before the wall? if you do so another time, I will lay hands on you. And from that time they came no more on the sabbath.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	22	I spoke also to the Levites that they should be purified, and should come to keep the gates, and to sanctify the sabbath day: for this also remember me, O my God, and spare me according to the multitude of thy tender mercies.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	23	In those days also I saw Jews that married wives, women of Azotus, and of Ammon, and of Moab.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	24	And their children spoke half in the speech of Azotus, and could not speak the Jews' language, but they spoke according to the language of this and that people.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	25	And I chid them, and laid my curse upon them. And I beat some of them, and shaved off their hair, and made them swear by God that they would not give their daughters to their sons, nor take their daughters for their sons, nor for themselves, saying:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	26	Did not Solomon king of Israel sin in this kind of thing? and surely among many nations, there was not a king like him, and he was beloved of his God, and God made him king over all Israel: and yet women of other countries brought even him to sin.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	27	And shall we also be disobedient and do all this great evil to transgress against our God, and marry strange women?
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	28	And one of the sons of Joiada the son of Eliasib the high priest, was son in law to Sanaballat the Horonite, and I drove him from me.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	29	Remember them, O Lord my God, that defile the priesthood, and the law of priests and Levites.
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	30	So I separated from them all strangers, and I appointed the courses of the priests and the Levites, every man in his ministry:
2 Esdras	Neh	16	13	31	And for the offering of wood at times appointed, and for the firstfruits: remember me, O my God, unto good. Amen.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	1	Tobias of the tribe and city of Nephtali, (which is in the upper parts of Galilee above Naasson, beyond the way that leadeth to the west, having on the right hand the city of Sephet,)
Tobias	Tob	17	1	2	When he was made captive in the days of Salmanasar king of the Assyrians, even in his captivity, forsook not the way of truth,
Tobias	Tob	17	1	3	But every day gave all he could get to his brethren his fellow captives, that were of his kindred.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	4	And when he was younger than any of the tribe of Nephtali, yet did he no childish thing in his work.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	5	Moreover when all went to the golden calves which Jeroboam king of Israel had made, he alone fled the company of all,
Tobias	Tob	17	1	6	And went to Jerusalem to the temple of the Lord, and there adored the Lord God of Israel, offering faithfully all his firstfruits, and his tithes,
Tobias	Tob	17	1	7	So that in the third year he gave all his tithes to the proselytes, and strangers.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	8	These and such like things did he observe when but a boy according to the law of God.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	9	But when he was a man, he took to wife Anna of his own tribe, and had a son by her, whom he called after his own name,
Tobias	Tob	17	1	10	And from his infancy he taught him to fear God, and to abstain from all sin.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	11	And when by the captivity he with his wife and his son and all his tribe was come to the city of Ninive,
Tobias	Tob	17	1	12	(When all ate of the meats of the Gentiles) he kept his soul and never was defiled with their meats.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	13	And because he was mindful of the Lord with all his heart, God gave him favour in the sight of Salmanasar the king.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	14	And he gave him leave to go whithersoever he would, with liberty to do whatever he had a mind.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	15	He therefore went to all that were in captivity, and gave them wholesome admonitions.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	16	And when he was come to Rages a city of the Medes, and had ten talents of silver of that with which he had been honoured by the king:
Tobias	Tob	17	1	17	And when amongst a great multitude of his kindred, he saw Gabelus in want, who was one of his tribe, taking a note of his hand he gave him the aforesaid sum of money.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	18	But after a long time, Salmanasar the king being dead, when Sennacherib his son, who reigned in his place, had a hatred for the children of Israel:
Tobias	Tob	17	1	19	Tobias daily went among all his kindred, and comforted them, and distributed to every one as he was able, out of his goods:
Tobias	Tob	17	1	20	He fed the hungry, and gave clothes to the naked, and was careful to bury the dead, and they that were slain.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	21	And when king Sennacherib was come back, fleeing from Judea by reason of the slaughter that God had made about him for his blasphemy, and being angry slew many of the children of Israel, Tobias buried their bodies.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	22	But when it was told the king, he commanded him to be slain, and took away all his substance.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	23	But Tobias fleeing naked away with his son and with his wife, lay concealed, for many loved him.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	24	But after forty-five days, the king was killed by his own sons.
Tobias	Tob	17	1	25	And Tobias returned to his house, and all his substance was restored to him.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	1	But after this, when there was a festival of the Lord, and a good dinner was prepared in Tobias's house,
Tobias	Tob	17	2	2	He said to his son: Go, and bring some of our tribe that fear God, to feast with us.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	3	And when he had gone, returning he told him, that one of the children of Israel lay slain in the street. And he forthwith leaped up from his place at the table, and left his dinner, and came fasting to the body:
Tobias	Tob	17	2	4	And taking it up carried it privately to his house, that after the sun was down, he might bury him cautiously.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	5	And when he had hid the body, he ate bread with mourning and fear,
Tobias	Tob	17	2	6	Remembering the word which the Lord spoke by Amos the prophet: Your festival days shall be turned into lamentation and mourning.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	7	So when the sun was down, he went and buried him.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	8	Now all his neighbours blamed him, saying: Once already commandment was given for thee to be slain because of this matter, and thou didst scarce escape the sentence of death, and dost thou again bury the dead?
Tobias	Tob	17	2	9	But Tobias fearing God more than the king, carried off the bodies of them that were slain, and hid them in his house, and at midnight buried them.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	10	Now it happened one day, that being wearied with burying, he came to his house, and cast himself down by the wall and slept,
Tobias	Tob	17	2	11	And as he was sleeping, hot dung out of a swallow's nest fell upon his eyes, and he was made blind.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	12	Now this trial the Lord therefore permitted to happen to him, that an example might be given to posterity of his patience, as also of holy Job.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	13	For whereas he had always feared God from his infancy, and kept his commandments, he repined not against God because the evil of blindness had befallen him,
Tobias	Tob	17	2	14	But continued immoveable in the fear of God, giving thanks to God all the days of his life.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	15	For as the kings insulted over holy Job: so his relations and kinsmen mocked at his life, saying:
Tobias	Tob	17	2	16	Where is thy hope, for which thou gavest alms, and buriedst the dead?
Tobias	Tob	17	2	17	But Tobias rebuked them, saying: Speak not so:
Tobias	Tob	17	2	18	For we are the children of the saints, and look for that life which God will give to those that never change their faith from him.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	19	Now Anna his wife went daily to weaving work, and she brought home what she could get for their living by the labour of her hands.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	20	Whereby it came to pass, that she received a young kid, and brought it home:
Tobias	Tob	17	2	21	And when her husband heard it bleating, he said: Take heed, lest perhaps it be stolen: restore ye it to its owners, for it is not lawful for us either to eat or to touch any thing that cometh by theft.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	22	At these words his wife being angry answered: It is evident thy hope is come to nothing, and thy alms now appear.
Tobias	Tob	17	2	23	And with these, and other such like words she upbraided him.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	1	Then Tobias sighed, and began to pray with tears,
Tobias	Tob	17	3	2	Saying: Thou art just, O Lord, and all thy judgments are just, and all thy ways mercy, and truth, and judgment:
Tobias	Tob	17	3	3	And now, O Lord, think of me, and take not revenge of my sins, neither remember my offenses, nor those of my parents.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	4	For we have not obeyed thy commandments, therefore are we delivered to spoil and to captivity, and death, and are made a fable, and a reproach to all nations, amongst which thou hast scattered us.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	5	And now, O Lord, great are thy judgments, because we have not done according to thy precepts, and have not walked sincerely before thee:
Tobias	Tob	17	3	6	And now, O Lord, do with me according to thy will, and command my spirit to be received in peace: for it is better for me to die, than to live.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	7	Now it happened on the same day, that Sara daughter of Raguel, in Rages a city of the Medes, received a reproach from one of her father's servant maids,
Tobias	Tob	17	3	8	Because she had been given to seven husbands, and a devil named Asmodeus had killed them, at their first going in unto her.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	9	So when she reproved the maid for her fault, she answered her, saying: May we never see son, or daughter of thee upon the earth, thou murderer of thy husbands.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	10	Wilt thou kill me also, as thou hast already killed seven husbands? At these words she went into an upper chamber of her house: and for three days and three nights did neither eat nor drink:
Tobias	Tob	17	3	11	But continuing in prayer with tears besought God, that he would deliver her from this reproach.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	12	And it came to pass on the third day, when she was making an end of her prayer, blessing the Lord,
Tobias	Tob	17	3	13	She said: Blessed is thy name, O God of our fathers: who when thou hast been angry, wilt shew mercy, and in the time of tribulation forgivest the sins of them that call upon thee.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	14	To thee, O Lord, I turn my face, to thee I direct my eyes.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	15	I beg, O Lord, that thou loose me from the bond of this reproach, or else take me away from the earth.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	16	Thou knowest, O Lord, that I never coveted a husband, and have kept my soul clean from all lust.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	17	Never have I joined myself with them that play: neither have I made myself partaker with them that walk in lightness.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	18	But a husband I consented to take, with thy fear, not with my lust.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	19	And either I was unworthy of them, or they perhaps were not worthy of me: because perhaps thou hast kept me for another man.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	20	For thy counsel is not in man's power.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	21	But this every one is sure of that worshippeth thee, that his life, if it be under trial, shall be crowned: and if it be under tribulation, it shall be delivered: and if it be under correction, it shall be allowed to come to thy mercy.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	22	For thou art not delighted in our being lost: because after a storm thou makest a calm, and after tears and weeping thou pourest in joyfulness.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	23	Be thy name, O God of Israel, blessed for ever.
Tobias	Tob	17	3	24	At that time the prayers of them both were heard in the sight of the glory of the most high God:
Tobias	Tob	17	3	25	And the holy angel of the Lord, Raphael was sent to heal them both, whose prayers at one time were rehearsed in the sight of the Lord.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	1	Therefore when Tobias thought that his prayer was heard that he might die, he called to him Tobias his son,
Tobias	Tob	17	4	2	And said to him: Hear, my son, the words of my mouth, and lay them as a foundation in thy heart.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	3	When God shall take my soul, thou shalt bury my body: and thou shalt honour thy mother all the days of her life:
Tobias	Tob	17	4	4	For thou must be mindful what and how great perils she suffered for thee in her womb.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	5	And when she also shall have ended the time of her life, bury her by me.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	6	And all the days of thy life have God in thy mind: and take heed thou never consent to sin, nor transgress the commandments of the Lord our God.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	7	Give alms out of thy substance, and turn not away thy face from any poor person: for so it shall come to pass that the face of the Lord shall not be turned from thee.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	8	According to thy ability be merciful.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	9	If thou have much give abundantly: if thou have a little, take care even so to bestow willingly a little.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	10	For thus thou storest up to thyself a good reward for the day of necessity.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	11	For alms deliver from all sin, and from death, and will not suffer the soul to go into darkness.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	12	Alms shall be a great confidence before the most high God, to all them that give it.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	13	Take heed to keep thyself, my son, from all fornication, and beside thy wife never endure to know a crime.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	14	Never suffer pride to reign in thy mind, or in thy words: for from it all perdition took its beginning.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	15	If any man hath done any work for thee, immediately pay him his hire, and let not the wages of thy hired servant stay with thee at all.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	16	See thou never do to another what thou wouldst hate to have done to thee by another.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	17	Eat thy bread with the hungry and the needy, and with thy garments cover the naked.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	18	Lay out thy bread, and thy wine upon the burial of a just man, and do not eat and drink thereof with the wicked.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	19	Seek counsel always of a wise man.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	20	Bless God at all times: and desire of him to direct thy ways, and that all thy counsels may abide in him.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	21	I tell thee also, my son, that I lent ten talents of silver, while thou wast yet a child, to Gabelus, in Rages a city of the Medes, and I have a note of his hand with me:
Tobias	Tob	17	4	22	Now therefore inquire how thou mayst go to him, and receive of him the foresaid sum of money, and restore to him the note of his hand.
Tobias	Tob	17	4	23	Fear not, my son: we lead indeed a poor life, but we shall have many good things if we fear God, and depart from all sin, and do that which is good.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	1	Then Tobias answered his father, and said: I will do all things, father, which thou hast commanded me.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	2	But how I shall get this money, I cannot tell; he knoweth me not, and I know not him: what token shall I give him? nor did I ever know the way which leadeth thither.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	3	Then his father answered him, and said: I have a note of his hand with me, which when thou shalt shew him, he will presently pay it.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	4	But go now, and seek thee out some faithful man, to go with thee for his hire: that thou mayst receive it, while I yet live.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	5	Then Tobias going forth, found a beautiful young man, standing girded, and as it were ready to walk.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	6	And not knowing that he was an angel of God, he saluted him, and said: From whence art thou, good young man?
Tobias	Tob	17	5	7	But he answered: Of the children of Israel. And Tobias said to him: Knowest thou the way that leadeth to the country of the Medes?
Tobias	Tob	17	5	8	And he answered: I know it: and I have often walked through all the ways thereof, and I have abode with Gabelus our brother, who dwelleth at Rages a city of the Medes, which is situate in the mount of Ecbatana.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	9	And Tobias said to him: Stay for me, I beseech thee, till I tell these same things to my father.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	10	Then Tobias going in told all these things to his father. Upon which his father being in admiration, desired that he would come in unto him.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	11	So going in he saluted him, and said: Joy be to thee always.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	12	And Tobias said: What manner of joy shall be to me, who sit in darkness, and see not the light of heaven?
Tobias	Tob	17	5	13	And the young man said to him: Be of good courage, thy cure from God is at hand.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	14	And Tobias said to him: Canst thou conduct my son to Gabelus at Rages, a city of the Medes? and when thou shalt return, I will pay thee thy hire.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	15	And the angel said to him: I will conduct him thither, and bring him back to thee.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	16	And Tobias said to him: I pray thee, tell me, of what family, or what tribe art thou?
Tobias	Tob	17	5	17	And Raphael the angel answered: Dost thou seek the family of him thou hirest, or the hired servant himself to go with thy son?
Tobias	Tob	17	5	18	But lest I should make thee uneasy, I am Azarias the son of the great Ananias.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	19	And Tobias answered: Thou art of a great family. But I pray thee be not angry that I desired to know thy family.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	20	And the angel said to him: I will lead thy son safe, and bring him to thee again safe.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	21	And Tobias answering, said: May you have a good journey, and God be with you in your way, and his angel accompany you.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	22	Then all things being ready, that were to be carried in their journey, Tobias bade his father and his mother farewell, and they set out both together.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	23	And when they were departed, his mother began to weep, and to say: Thou hast taken the staff of our old age, and sent him away from us.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	24	I wish the money for which thou hast sent him, had never been.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	25	For poverty was sufficient for us, that we might account it as riches, that we saw our son.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	26	And Tobias said to her: Weep not, our son will arrive thither safe, and will return safe to us, and thy eyes shall see him.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	27	For I believe that the good angel of God doth accompany him, and doth order all things well that are done about him, so that he shall return to us with joy.
Tobias	Tob	17	5	28	At these words his mother ceased weeping, and held her peace.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	1	And Tobias went forward, and the dog followed him, and he lodged the first night by the river of Tigris.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	2	And he went out to wash his feet, and behold a monstrous fish came up to devour him.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	3	And Tobias being afraid of him, cried out with a loud voice, saying: Sir, he cometh upon me.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	4	And the angel said to him: Take him by the gill, and draw him to thee. And when he had done so, he drew him out upon the land, and he began to pant before his feet.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	5	Then the angel said to him: Take out the entrails of the fish, and lay up his heart, and his gall, and his liver for thee: for these are necessary for useful medicines.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	6	And when he had done so, he roasted the flesh thereof, and they took it with them in the way: the rest they salted as much as might serve them, till they came to Rages the city of the Medes.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	7	Then Tobias asked the angel, and said to him: I beseech thee, brother Azarias, tell me what remedies are these things good for, which thou hast bid me keep of the fish?
Tobias	Tob	17	6	8	And the angel, answering, said to him: If thou put a little piece of its heart upon coals, the smoke thereof driveth away all kind of devils, either from man or from woman, so that they come no more to them.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	9	And the gall is good for anointing the eyes, in which there is a white speck, and they shall be cured.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	10	And Tobias said to him: Where wilt thou that we lodge?
Tobias	Tob	17	6	11	And the angel answering, said: Here is one whose name is Raguel, a near kinsman of thy tribe, and he hath a daughter named Sara, but he hath no son nor any other daughter beside her.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	12	All his substance is due to thee, and thou must take her to wife.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	13	Ask her therefore of her father, and he will give her thee to wife.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	14	Then Tobias answered, and said: I hear that she hath been given to seven husbands, and they all died: moreover I have heard, that a devil killed them.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	15	Now I am afraid, lest the same thing should happen to me also: and whereas I am the only child of my parents, I should bring down their old age with sorrow to hell.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	16	Then the angel Raphael said to him: Hear me, and I will shew thee who they are, over whom the devil can prevail.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	17	For they who in such manner receive matrimony, as to shut out God from themselves, and from their mind, and to give themselves to their lust, as the horse and mule, which have not understanding, over them the devil hath power.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	18	But thou when thou shalt take her, go into the chamber, and for three days keep thyself continent from her, and give thyself to nothing else but to prayers with her.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	19	And on that night lay the liver of the fish on the fire, and the devil shall be driven away.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	20	But the second night thou shalt be admitted into the society of the holy Patriarchs.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	21	And the third night thou shalt obtain a blessing that sound children may be born of you.
Tobias	Tob	17	6	22	And when the third night is past, thou shalt take the virgin with the fear of the Lord, moved rather for love of children than for lust, that in the seed of Abraham thou mayst obtain a blessing in children.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	1	And they went in to Raguel, and Raguel received them with joy.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	2	And Raguel looking upon Tobias, said to Anna his wife: How like is this young man to my cousin?
Tobias	Tob	17	7	3	And when he had spoken these words, he said: Whence are ye young men our brethren?
Tobias	Tob	17	7	4	But they said: We are of the tribe of Nephtali, of the captivity of Ninive.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	5	And Raguel said to them: Do you know Tobias my brother? And they said: We know him.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	6	And when he was speaking many good things of him, the angel said to Raguel: Tobias concerning whom thou inquirest is this young man's father.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	7	And Raguel went to him, and kissed him with tears, and weeping upon his neck, said: A blessing be upon thee, my son, because thou art the son of a good and most virtuous man.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	8	And Anna his wife, and Sara their daughter wept.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	9	And after they had spoken, Raguel commanded a sheep to be killed, and a feast to be prepared. And when he desired them to sit down to dinner,
Tobias	Tob	17	7	10	Tobias said: I will not eat nor drink here this day, unless thou first grant me my petition, and promise to give me Sara thy daughter.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	11	Now when Raguel heard this he was afraid, knowing what had happened to those seven husbands, that went in unto her: and he began to fear lest it might happen to him also in like manner: and as he was in suspense, and gave no answer to his petition,
Tobias	Tob	17	7	12	The angel said to him: Be not afraid to give her to this man, for to him who feareth God is thy daughter due to be his wife: therefore another could not have her.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	13	Then Raguel said: I doubt not but God hath regarded my prayers and tears in his sight.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	14	And I believe he hath therefore made you come to me, that this maid might be married to one of her own kindred, according to the law of Moses: and now doubt not but I will give her to thee.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	15	And taking the right hand of his daughter, he gave it into the right hand of Tobias, saying: The God of Abraham, and the God of Isaac, and the God of Jacob be with you, and may he join you together, and fulfill his blessing in you.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	16	And taking paper they made a writing of the marriage.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	17	And afterwards they made merry, blessing God.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	18	And Raguel called to him Anna his wife, and bade her prepare another chamber.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	19	And she brought Sara her daughter in thither, and she wept.
Tobias	Tob	17	7	20	And she said to her: Be of good cheer, my daughter: the Lord of heaven give thee joy for the trouble thou hast undergone.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	1	And after they had supped, they brought in the young man to her.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	2	And Tobias remembering the angel's word, took out of his bag part of the liver, and laid it upon burning coals.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	3	Then the angel Raphael took the devil, and bound him in the desert of upper Egypt.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	4	Then Tobias exhorted the virgin, and said to her: Sara, arise, and let us pray to God today, and tomorrow, and the next day: because for these three nights we are joined to God: and when the third night is over, we will be in our own wedlock.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	5	For we are the children of saints, and we must not be joined together like heathens that know not God.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	6	So they both arose, and prayed earnestly both together that health might be given them,
Tobias	Tob	17	8	7	And Tobias said: Lord God of our father, may the heavens and the earth, and the sea, and the fountains, and the rivers, and all thy creatures that are in them, bless thee.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	8	Thou madest Adam of the slime of the earth, and gavest him Eve for a helper.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	9	And now, Lord, thou knowest, that not for fleshly lust do I take my sister to wife, but only for the love of posterity, in which thy name may be blessed for ever and ever.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	10	Sara also said: Have mercy on us, O Lord, have mercy on us, and let us grow old both together in health.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	11	And it came to pass about the cockcrowing, Raguel ordered his servants to be called for, and they went with him together to dig a grave.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	12	For he said: Lest perhaps it may have happened to him, in like manner as it did to the other seven husbands, that went in unto her.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	13	And when they had prepared the pit, Raguel went back to his wife, and said to her:
Tobias	Tob	17	8	14	Send one of thy maids, and let her see if he be dead, that I may bury him before it be day.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	15	So she sent one of her maidservants, who went into the chamber, and found them safe and sound, sleeping both together.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	16	And returning she brought the good news: and Raguel and Anna his wife blessed the Lord,
Tobias	Tob	17	8	17	And said: We bless thee, O Lord God of Israel, because it hath not happened as we suspected.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	18	For thou hast shewn thy mercy to us, and hast shut out from us the enemy that persecuted us.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	19	And thou hast taken pity upon two only children. Make them, O Lord, bless thee more fully: and to offer up to thee a sacrifice of thy praise, and of their health, that all nations may know, that thou alone art God in all the earth.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	20	And immediately Raguel commanded his servants, to fill up the pit they had made, before it was day.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	21	And he spoke to his wife to make ready a feast, and prepare all kind of provisions that are necessary for such as go a journey.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	22	He caused also two fat kine, and four wethers to be killed, and a banquet to be prepared for all his neighbours, and all his friends.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	23	And Raguel adjured Tobias, to abide with him two weeks.
Tobias	Tob	17	8	24	And of all things which Raguel possessed, he gave one half to Tobias, and made him a writing, that the half that remained should after their decease come also to Tobias.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	1	Then Tobias called the angel to him, whom he took to be a man, and said to him: Brother Azarias, I pray thee hearken to my words:
Tobias	Tob	17	9	2	If I should give myself to be thy servant I should not make a worthy return for thy care.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	3	However, I beseech thee, to take with thee beasts and servants, and to go to Gabelus to Rages the city of the Medes: and to restore to him his note of hand, and receive of him the money, and desire him to come to my wedding.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	4	For thou knowest that my father numbereth the days: and if I stay one day more, his soul will be afflicted.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	5	And indeed thou seest how Raguel hath adjured me, whose adjuring I cannot despise.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	6	Then Raphael took four of Raguel's servants, and two camels, and went to Rages the city of the Medes: and finding Gabelus, gave him his note of hand, and received of him all the money.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	7	And he told him concerning Tobias the son of Tobias, all that had been done: and made him come with him to the wedding.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	8	And when he was come into Raguel's house he found Tobias sitting at the table: and he leaped up, and they kissed each other: and Gabelus wept, and blessed God,
Tobias	Tob	17	9	9	And said: The God of Israel bless thee, because thou art the son of a very good and just man, and that feareth God, and doth almsdeeds:
Tobias	Tob	17	9	10	And may a blessing come upon thy wife and upon your parents.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	11	And may you see your children, and your children's children, unto the third and fourth generation: and may your seed be blessed by the God of Israel, who reigneth for ever and ever.
Tobias	Tob	17	9	12	And when all had said, Amen, they went to the feast: but the marriage feast they celebrated also with the fear of the Lord.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	1	But as Tobias made longer stay upon occasion of the marriage, Tobias his father was solicitous, saying: Why thinkest thou doth my son tarry, or why is he detained there?
Tobias	Tob	17	10	2	Is Gabelus dead, thinkest thou, and no man will pay him the money?
Tobias	Tob	17	10	3	And he began to be exceeding sad, both he and Anna his wife with him: and they began both to weep together: because their son did not return to them on the day appointed.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	4	But his mother wept and was quite disconsolate, and said: Woe, woe is me, my son; why did we send thee to go to a strange country, the light of our eyes, the staff of our old age, the comfort of our life, the hope of our posterity?
Tobias	Tob	17	10	5	We having all things together in thee alone, ought not to have let thee go from us.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	6	And Tobias said to her: Hold thy peace, and be not troubled, our son is safe: that man with whom we sent him is very trusty.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	7	But she could by no means be comforted, but daily running out looked round about, and went into all the ways by which there seemed any hope he might return, that she might if possible see him coming afar off.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	8	But Raguel said to his son in law: Stay here, and I will send a messenger to Tobias thy father, that thou art in health.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	9	And Tobias said to him: I know that my father and mother now count the days, and their spirit is grievously afflicted within them.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	10	And when Raguel had pressed Tobias with many words, and he by no means would hearken to him, he delivered Sara unto him, and half of all his substance in menservants, and womenservants, in cattle, in camels, and in kine, and in much money, and sent him away safe and joyful from him.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	11	Saying: The holy angel of the Lord be with you in your journey, and bring you through safe, and that you may find all things well about your parents, and my eyes see your children before I die.
Tobias	Tob	17	10	12	And the parents taking their daughter kissed her, and let her go:
Tobias	Tob	17	10	13	Admonishing her to honour her father and mother in law, to love her husband, to take care of the family, to govern the house, and to behave herself irreprehensibly.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	1	And as they were returning they came to Charan, which is in the midway to Ninive, the eleventh day.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	2	And the angel said: Brother Tobias, thou knowest how thou didst leave thy father.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	3	If it please thee therefore, let us go before, and let the family follow softly after us, together with thy wife, and with the beasts.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	4	And as this their going pleased him, Raphael said to Tobias: Take with thee of the gall of the fish, for it will be necessary. So Tobias took some of that gall and departed.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	5	But Anna sat beside the way daily, on the top of a hill, from whence she might see afar off.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	6	And while she watched his coming from that place, she saw him afar off, and presently perceived it was her son coming: and returning she told her husband, saying: Behold thy son cometh.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	7	And Raphael said to Tobias: As soon as thou shalt come into thy house, forthwith adore the Lord thy God: and giving thanks to him, go to thy father, and kiss him.
Tobias	Tob	17	11	8	And immediately anoint his eyes with this gall of the fish, which thou carriest with thee. For be assured that his eyes shall be presently opened, and thy father shall see the light of heaven, and shall rejoice in the sight of thee.
